{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e","id":1285472,"title":"Mortals in 3e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-06T21:22:04-08:00","id":1285472,"title":"Mortals in 3e","content":"I know that this might be a somewhat contentious topic, given the lack of Enlightened mortals in 3e, but given that the exalted seem to be substantially less than 1% of the population, and there are so many threats to mortal life it seems improbable that humans survive given the frankly minimal protection that ~30,000 Dragon-blooded can give them. But even in 2e, enlightened mortals were a rare occurrence. This also bothers me since even animals seem to be able to gain access to the essence and thus a limited number of charms, and they can do it more easily than mortals can. So I wanted to make a list of ways that mortals can gain access to enough supernatural mojo to plausibly punch above their weight class (they don't need to be an even match, just a threat). <br /> <br /> Note: I am focusing on combat power because it has a simple 'win condition' but any type of power is valid.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Magical Learning</b></u> <br /> This category is defined by anything that any mortal character can gain access to, and that they don't require others to help them. This does not need to be literal learning, if there is an artifact or manse that can grant them powers, which they could seek out on their own then it goes here.<ul><li>Martial Enlightenment - This may not be a thing anymore, but in 2e mortals could reach a max of Essence 3 and learn terrestrial martial arts charms. They had a max of 30 personal motes.</li> <li>Sorcerous Enlightenment - This is definitely still a thing and with a decent shaping ritual, and possibly and infernal artifact it may be the most dangerous tool available to mortals. Bind a few demons, have a sorcerous pool ready before the fight and see what you can accomplish.</li> </ul><u><b>Heritage</b></u><br /> This category is for abilities that you either were born with, or you don't have them. Though they might be able to be improved on through effort and training.<ul><li>God-blooded: Most gods, and thus god-blooded aren't that powerful. However, you could have the bastard child of a fairly powerful god, like Ahlat, which could learn their powers and potentially be able to spike above Dragonblooded power for short periods of time, though they probably can't maintain that exertion long. I also wonder if a god-blooded has the potential to achieve apotheosis and become a god under their parent's purview.</li> <li>Demon-blooded: Exactly like god-blooded, but with demons. Their power would clearly depend a lot on the power of their demonic sire - one of the many children born from Neomah might be able to do some body-alteration tricks and some social mojo beyond their ken. Whereas, a hypothetical child of Liger would be either a menace or a boon to all the world.</li> <li>Exalted Parentage: We have heard that the children of exalted may be special in some way, but that it will be different than merely gaining access to their parent's charms. Clearly not a thing for Dragonblooded.<ul><li>Beastmen - the way Beastmen were made in prior editions was... unpleasant, especially in large numbers. This also isn't necessarily 'magic' in that it's unknown what it will entail in this edition, and may not grant any charms whatsoever. However, Beastmen are generally more dangerous than pure mortals.</li> </ul></li> <li>Fae-blooded: Unlike the Inheritance above, at this point, we are starting to scrape the dregs of inherited power. Like the others, they have a non-mortal parent from whom they can inherit supernatural abilities. However the Fae abilities tend toward the weird/illusionary already, and many only really function in the Wyld. I suspect that a Fae-blooded might be instrumental to a moral adventuring party, but mainly because they can protect them from the ravages of the Wyld.</li> <li>Ghostblooded: I don't even really know how this is supposed to work, but apparently a ghost can impregnate someone or be impregnated, in spitting in the face of all laws of life and nature. Ghostblooded inherits their parent's power, which unless they were a ghost of some significance, like a Deathlord or Nephwrack, this would be pretty meager.</li> </ul><u><b>Patronage</b></u><br /> This category is not innate power, it must be sought out after birth and it cannot be gained through effort or merit. It can only be gained through the beneficence of a greater power of some sort, and likely at great cost. I am excluding all exalted, who are no longer relevantly 'mortal' (though currently there is little reason that there can't be an arbitrary number of Liminal and Exigent Exalts).<ul><li>Endowment - there used to be rules in 2e that Gods could 'adopt mortals' and endow them with god-blood and thus charms. I suspect with the introduction of Exigence, this will be dropped.</li> <li>Solar-Mentorship: I vaguely remember a charm that granted a mortal ally the use of a Solar charm, though obviously a basic one.</li> <li>Infernal-forging: though it didn't give access to any charms, 2e had many infernal charms that allowed them to mutate mortals to their needs. Much like regular mutation mechanically, but guided so there are no downsides, so long as you trust the patron.</li> <li>Kalediscopic Border of Creation - there was an attack that would grant the target a temporary +10 successes on all actions for a limited time, followed by an eternity of cursed ineptitude.</li> <li>Investiture of Infernal Glory - though there isn't a template for it this time, this was the biggest bang for your buck in terms of magic power, but with the downside to compensate. For exalted it lets them jump 1 rung on the power scale for martial arts and Sorcery, as well as granting them access to powerful Infernal charms.<ul><li>The effects for mortals and DB are a bit less clear, it clearly grants them access to terrestrial and celestial circles of power respectively. But since they can both get that power naturally through the Root of the Perfected Lotus or Immaculate Mastery and a variety of artifacts, it unclear if this could bootstrap Mortals all the way to Celestial Power and make them a match for young Solars. The presence of an artifact for the Scarlet Empress that allows her to use Adamant Sorcery suggests that it might be possible, but that it would require a second form of investment, such as an artifact which would be unlikely for a mortal.</li> <li>Given that Akuma-hood functions like a mini-infernal exaltation in many ways, and the fact that there is little in the way of Akuma being mass produced beyond what a terrible deal it is and Sidereal crackdowns it really points to how much potential there could be if the Yozi weren't such terrible rulers.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Desultory</b></u><br /> This is a category of power for all abilities that are gained randomly, or uncontrollably. They may even be largely detrimental.<ul><li>Wyld Mutation - Randomized mutations from exposure to the wyld.</li> <li>Infernal Mutations - Similar to wyld mutations, but they likely differ in what types of changes that can be granted.</li> <li>Serendipity - Just from the antagonist section there appear to be a number of bizarre events or features that can grant people magical abilities from the minor to the Celestial, but that they often irrevocably change the person exposed, possibly to the point where they are no longer the same person.</li> </ul>Are there any there any sources that I am missing? As a side note, how do people feel about the loss of enlightened mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T22:02:50-08:00","id":1285479,"title":"","content":"Okay, two things:<br /> <br /> One, who is trying to kill everybody in the world?<br /> <br /> Two, for the majority of human history, many if not most people did not live past the age of five (there's a fairly good chance that your grandparents, and almost certain one for your great-grandparents, had siblings that did not survive childhood), and thereafter you had pretty good odds of dying prematurely as a result of infection, disease, malnutrition or starvation, severe weather, natural disasters and war. You can kind of infer what the mortality rate was like from the fact that, in the hundred or so years since decent technology was developed and implemented to deal with most of that, the human population increased by about three times as much as it had managed to reach after about ten thousand years. Like hey, look at how many people are not dying of polio and tuberculosis anymore.<br /> <br /> People still managed. They lived with it. What else were they going to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T22:29:22-08:00","id":1285481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285479#post1285479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, two things:<br /> <br /> One, who is trying to kill everybody in the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, of the Thousand Dooms, the only remaining one unambiguously remaining is the Fair Folk, yeah? They still want to destroy Creation and watch it boil away into the Wyld? There are probably still Underworld shenanigans that are apocalypse-related going on, but that's yet to be at all confirmed.<br /> <br /> I'm going to flip one of the OP's contentions around:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it seems improbable that humans survive given the frankly minimal protection that ~30,000 Dragon-blooded can give them. </div> </div> </div>There are certainly some threats that the un-Exalted are not equipped at all to deal with (I don't think humanity could have toppled the Yozis, even with divine aid, without some among their number becoming Exalted) but to speak bluntly: the Dragon-Blooded are not more powerful, as a class, than the un-Exalted masses are. If the un-Exalted rose up against the Dragon-Blooded, many of them would die but the teeming millions of Creation, many of whom are wise, strong, cunning, and just plain tough-as-nails themselves, would pull down the Dragon-Blooded just as the Dragon-Blooded pulled down the Solars.<br /> <br /> Don't approach things from the standpoint of &quot;mortals are pets. Sometimes a pet can rip out someones throat, but ultimately: pets. They live under the aegis of the Exalted, who are the only true power in the world.&quot; This is not so. The Exalted are earth-shaking heroes and there are some threats only they can deal with, but each and every one of them was un-Exalted once, and there's not a single one of them, in 3E, who can't be pulled off their horse and murdered by a sufficient number of determined mortals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T22:46:35-08:00","id":1285486,"title":"","content":"Gone actually start my day soon so some notes: <br /> Animals having charms was mentioned here and another thread, and uh...those are powered by the Exalted through familiar charms. Not by the animal.<br /> <br /> Missing sources of power include: <br /> Whatever the fuck is going on with the Yenin<br /> Numbers<br /> Tactics <br /> Secret techniques(that one Adversary has a soul cobra)<br /> Artifacts That allow mortal attunement (looking at you vainglory)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T22:47:42-08:00","id":1285487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285479#post1285479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, two things:<br /> <br /> One, who is trying to kill everybody in the world?<br /> <br /> Two, for the majority of human history, many if not most people did not live past the age of five (there's a fairly good chance that your grandparents, and almost certain one for your great-grandparents, had siblings that did not survive childhood), and thereafter you had pretty good odds of dying prematurely as a result of infection, disease, malnutrition or starvation, severe weather, natural disasters and war. You can kind of infer what the mortality rate was like from the fact that, in the hundred or so years since decent technology was developed and implemented to deal with most of that, the human population increased by about three times as much as it had managed to reach after about ten thousand years. Like hey, look at how many people are not dying of polio and tuberculosis anymore.<br /> <br /> People still managed. They lived with it. What else were they going to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I understand the meaning in your reply. After all the Neverborn, most of the Deathlords, and a good portion of the abyssals want to wipe out mortals. Not to mention their Nephwracks and various other undead minions. The Yozi that don't want to enslave humanity or make them exist in a state of constant torment have omnicide on the menu. Their respective Akuma literally have to be on board. The demons are a mixed bag, but some are on board with the Zero-Mortals plan. There are the Behemoths, the Heckeronherie, various other malevolent monsters. All of the Raksha want to drag creation back to formlessness. Also probably at least a few of the Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> None of the factor that contributed to human death prior to the modern era were gunning to kill everyone. Diseases may kill us, but this is usually an unintentional side-effect of their lifecycle, not the goal. Imagine if you would, if the black plague was sentient, and could plan and coordinate its actions and had the goal of wiping out all mankind. How successful do you think it would have been? I don't know if it would have succeeded, but I wouldn't be comfortable betting against it either.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking that mortal life be made easy or simple, arguably the existence of god-blooded would complicate and endanger mortal hierarchies even more. Also, I should probably clarify that my main issue is that while in some ways mortals are more dangerous and powerful than ever, especially in groups, in other ways they are less consequential as individuals. The lack of enlightened mortals makes it feel like a mortal can't accomplish much of note unless they exalt, which is kind of shitty.<br /> <br /> Edit: Lastly I should have clarified, I am currently making a new exalted wiki for fan content, and I wanted to make sure I wasn't missing anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","user":"Nabirius","date":". 02-07-2019, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T22:49:30-08:00","id":1285488,"title":"","content":"I'd like to say that while I similarly think that mortal heroes can accomplish amazing things on their own, even in the magical world of exalted, I think this is a cool list! Especially since an army of mortals could also be lead by any of these individuals. It's also good fodder to give some mortal antagonists some punch. For DBs mortals can be pretty genuinely scary in certain situations, and for Solars mortal minions can be a good big bad supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T23:00:59-08:00","id":1285490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think, of the Thousand Dooms, the only remaining one unambiguously remaining is the Fair Folk, yeah? They still want to destroy Creation and watch it boil away into the Wyld? There are probably still Underworld shenanigans that are apocalypse-related going on, but that's yet to be at all confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, laying aside #NotAllFairFolk, the original query seems more predicated on the extinction of humanity being an aggregate thing, rather than a singular effort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but to speak bluntly: the Dragon-Blooded are not more powerful, as a class, than the un-Exalted masses are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's somewhat true, but missing some of the ways in which Dragon Blooded can apply their powers more laterally.<br /> <br /> I think the original poster is overlooking the same thing towards a different purpose, frankly.<br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded aren't going to look very effective if one is approaching them as each needing to personally defend a large number of people, but if they're applying themselves to creating and sustaining systems that widely and efficiently project power, they get some force multipliers.<br /> <br /> Plus a few things that really are a bit overwhelming. Can somebody remind me what the Earth Signature for Bureaucracy does?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the un-Exalted rose up against the Dragon-Blooded, many of them would die but the teeming millions of Creation, many of whom are wise, strong, cunning, and just plain tough-as-nails themselves, would pull down the Dragon-Blooded just as the Dragon-Blooded pulled down the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, when there's a lot more of them, that becomes a harder prospect just from organizational inefficiency.<br /> <br /> Then you add in things like Exalted heritage being widespread enough that they're periodically popping back up.<br /> <br /> Or trying to kill a Water Aspect who lives near the sea and knows when to fold 'em. What, is the baying mob going to dive in after them?<br /> <br /> Anyway, the best defence a lot of mortals have is probably convincing the thing threatening them that it would profit more from letting them live, or convincing somebody else to fight on their behalf. This probably often involves a lot of canniness and cunning.<br /> <br /> And it won't work a lot of the time. Again, what is the population growth rate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T23:33:25-08:00","id":1285494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285487#post1285487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that I understand the meaning in your reply. After all the Neverborn, most of the Deathlords, and a good portion of the abyssals want to wipe out mortals. Not to mention their Nephwracks and various other undead minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Neverborn are largely impotent, the Deathlords are... complicated, the Abyssals have only been around five years (and also complicated) and the Nephwracks have that pesky problem of turning into ash in direct sunlight.<br /> <br /> Also, they hardly really have nukes. The best methods most can employ are ultimately not much better than what has been employed historically.<br /> <br /> &quot;But what about the Great Contagion?&quot; Well, it can't be stopped by enlightened mortals, so it's a moot point anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yozi that don't want to enslave humanity or make them exist in a state of constant torment have omnicide on the menu. Their respective Akuma literally have to be on board. The demons are a mixed bag, but some are on board with the Zero-Mortals plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yozis are trapped outside the world for all eternity. Most demons aren't into that shit, and wouldn't have the power to do it if they were. <br /> <br /> How many akuma do you imagine them to have, and what are their capabilities?<br /> <br /> The point of me saying that nobody really has nukes before is that, without that, killing lots of people deliberately takes a really long time. Time for people to see it coming and run away. Time for opposition to mobilise. How many people does this company of akuma Exalted on an omnicidal crusade kill before, say, the Sidereals come down on them? They're not killbots, the Yozis can't just build more of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are the Behemoths, the Heckeronherie, various other malevolent monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hekatonchires are stuck in the Underworld, if many of them even act like this. Most behemoths are basically just walking natural disasters or really big animals as far as their scope or motive. Most aren't deliberately attacking people, and population densities have to be low enough that their casualty rates aren't very big.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the Raksha want to drag creation back to formlessness.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't, and Raksha of all political affiliations are a shattered remnant of the forces that tried to destroy the world (and whose failure to do so was not because enlightened mortals stopped them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also probably at least a few of the Celestial Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can make any argument work if you include unsubstantiated made up details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine if you would, if the black plague was sentient, and could plan and coordinate its actions and had the goal of wiping out all mankind. How successful do you think it would have been? I don't know if it would have succeeded, but I wouldn't be comfortable betting against it either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Atlantic and Pacific oceans would have presented a significant obstacle.<br /> <br /> And hey, if they're wiping out Afro-Eurasian humanity, they're also killing off shit like smallpox. Americans eventually grow numerous enough to start colonising the vast, empty continents. Interesting alternative timeline.<br /> <br /> I kid of course. The continents won't be empty; there will be people who isolated themselves from the plague.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">in other ways they are less consequential as individuals. The lack of enlightened mortals makes it feel like a mortal can't accomplish much of note unless they exalt, which is kind of shitty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who among us is consequential as an individual? What accomplishments do you want a given mortal to have? What is stopping them?<br /> <br /> Say a mortal character writes an RPG. For the sake of argument, let's assume that an Exalt who has the same interest will definitely produce a superior one, or at least a more successful one. Is an accomplishment worthless because it isn't the best around?<br /> <br /> If it is, why are any of us having this conversation?<br /> <br /> (Meaning no disrespect to the game)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Lastly I should have clarified, I am currently making a new exalted wiki for fan content, and I wanted to make sure I wasn't missing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T23:38:40-08:00","id":1285495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, of the Thousand Dooms, the only remaining one unambiguously remaining is the Fair Folk, yeah? They still want to destroy Creation and watch it boil away into the Wyld? ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no. Fair Folk are as I gather last, not going back to the version that was in the 1e book. Remember a bit that the Fair Folk as a potentail existential threat was in part from authors going off the rails on following an outline (see <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:secret-history-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for more on that). While there might be Fair Folk who think that, the general vibe that we got in late 2e and I think we're going to see with the hannya still being a thing, we're going to get the raksha-as-refugees thing still. Some might still very want another Balorian Crusade, but they probably ultimatley don't matter in the general long term survival of the human species.<br /> <br /> Generally too, raksha while like, not unheard of, aren't something yous ee every day. Most people in Creaiton are afraid of a bad harvest or invading armies more than fairies. Fair Folk are a really nasty disastor, probably akin to a hurricane, invading army, or plague. But humanity deals with those too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... There are probably still Underworld shenanigans that are apocalypse-related going on, but that's yet to be at all confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually skeptical it'll ever be the case since apocalyptic-level plots are not conductive to intersting setting building, and the current devs are keen more I think on making Creation interesting and a focus. When you introduce existential threats, things like armies and wars stop being as important.<br /> <br /> Simply put, the sort of things that humans care about day to day in Creation are probably what folks have cared about day-to-day on Earth for most of history. THe list of potential disasters that could hurt your life are longer, but that they happen to be sapient doesn't mean that humanity is at some risk of exitinction every moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T00:07:57-08:00","id":1285498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285487#post1285487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know that I understand the meaning in your reply. After all the Neverborn, most of the Deathlords, and a good portion of the abyssals want to wipe out mortals. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Neverborn don't want anything. They're asleep and impotent at the bottom of the Underworld. There is also something in other outlets that there's no Oblivion anymore anyhow. The Neverborn are dead gods thrashing in their sleep and the Deathlords are powerful ghosts who wrestled packs from them after centuries fo work. The Neverborn wanting anything is irrelevant and the Deahtlords seem to be pretty happy ruling their domains for as long as they can. Mask of Winters just as much likes <i>toying with</i> mortals as he likes killing them, as an example.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are a diverse group of people with their own goals, a more student-master relationship with the practical deities fo the Underwolrd the Deathlords have become and so on. Probably a lot of them have other interests besides omnicdie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Not to mention their Nephwracks and various other undead minions. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been nephwracks of some sort probably since the dawn of time and the world seems to do fine even when there were multiple civil wars, an Usupration, and a Contagion. If they were an existential threat to humanity, they'd of shown to be the case. They probably are again, pretty rare in the grand scheme of things people actually worry about in Creation compared to say, cholera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... The Yozi that don't want to enslave humanity or make them exist in a state of constant torment have omnicide on the menu. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>They Yozis will never get out and their souls are not interested in fulfilling thier revenge. They will thrash uselessly at their cage for the rest of all time because of the pacts they made. The thing folks will most likely interact with are their souls, which range from pretty magnanamous about Hell (Ligier), alien in want (Munaxes) or uninterested in people until called to deal with them (Erembour). And things get more diverging from there. And many aren't that murdeorus to my understanding. Just angry. And again, while Creaiton is a pretty magical place, actual human-demon interactions is probably rare enough that folks just prioritize other things quite often. Demons are dangerous and disasterous to people and could destory kingdoms. But the world is not in any eminent threat of demonic destruction. Again, it hasn't for thousands of years now, and it probably won't be soon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Their respective Akuma literally have to be on board. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Akuma in 3e aren't what they were before. Akuma is a catch-all term for Exalts who have made some deal for power from Hell. Being an infernalist might be that youg ot some sorcery or you turned into something like Dukantha. But they are still probably rare amongst a group that save Dragon-Blooded, number only in the hundreds. Many akuma have independence enough to not have to worry about such things and any who are just murdershitbots are are so vanishingly rare that they're not something that'll end the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... The demons are a mixed bag, but some are on board with the Zero-Mortals plan. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no real Zero Mortals plan to my understanidng. Most demons seem to not give a shit about anything out of Hell or their weird projects and amny are actually quite fond of humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are the Behemoths, the Heckeronherie, various other malevolent monsters. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation has had these since Ever. As noted already, most behemoths are just exotic geography, disasters or animals. They are rare, and dangerous, the things you hear legends about. Creation is more like Flat Earth, where these things eventually get spun out and folks think might even be overblown even if the world is known to be magical. Not One Punch Man where there's a new levelling of City Z ever week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...All of the Raksha want to drag creation back to formlessness. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>First, no they don't. Most raksha at this point are at best refugee nobles in a lost land. The hannya prowl their original origins and their best effort to do this died wiht Balor. And note, this never happened before him either in the way it did. Fair Folk are like demons, the dead, a storm, plague or army. They add to the list of human miseries in Creaiton, not overwhelm them existentially.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Also probably at least a few of the Celestial Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, what does a Celestial do that's so existential? Even Solar Circle Sorcery, while powerful, ultimatley is reginal in power I feel. An Exalt who really wants to break the world is probably rather rare, and those who have come close something that draws in the not-mortals enough in the coruse of hsitory to not be something mortals worrya bout. Again, cholera matters than some hypothetical one in billions maniac on the other side of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the factor that contributed to human death prior to the modern era were gunning to kill everyone. Diseases may kill us, but this is usually an unintentional side-effect of their lifecycle, not the goal. Imagine if you would, if the black plague was sentient, and could plan and coordinate its actions and had the goal of wiping out all mankind. How successful do you think it would have been? I don't know if it would have succeeded, but I wouldn't be comfortable betting against it either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a lot in Creation is that in a mood to kill people en masse either really. The entire idea that there's arrayed forces gunning to kill every last human is just something 3e doesn't worry about. This is because it's focused much more on the ways of people and their own issues. Existential threats make for bad setting building since it means a civil war or rising empire is irrelevant in the context of some &quot;real thrat' to all life. (It's bad fiction too. Infinity War is fun, but it ultimatley is going to have a bit of folks speculating about <i>how</i> they fix it, not whether, becuase when you make stakes like that and want a continued story, the soltuion is forgone.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not asking that mortal life be made easy or simple, arguably the existence of god-blooded would complicate and endanger mortal hierarchies even more. Also, I should probably clarify that my main issue is that while in some ways mortals are more dangerous and powerful than ever, especially in groups, in other ways they are less consequential as individuals. The lack of enlightened mortals makes it feel like a mortal can't accomplish much of note unless they exalt, which is kind of shitty.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only becuase you've stacked the deck with so many actually rare events that it necessitates things. A big thing to remember is that Creation in 3e is <i>not</i> in the existential threat it was in 2e. I mean, think on number of Exalts even. Through most of human history, there hasn't been many more Exalts than there are now. There have even been instances of mass die-off, probably like the Solar-Lunar war in the early eras, the fall of the First Deliberative, all that. Through all this time there have been hundreds of human socities, empires, cities, peoples, tribes, wars, conflicts, alliances, and so on. I think a big thign to remember is that while the Exalted are impactful, they are sitll very impactful indivduals in a very big world. When you basically say the only things out there are out ot kill humanity, and then that fighting htose constantly are the only things that matter ultiamtely, it's ignoring the fact that Creation seeems to like, actually operate with what appears to be less of that around in order for the setting ot make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T00:10:59-08:00","id":1285499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285494#post1285494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Levi, there is literally no reason for your hostility and condescension.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://exalted-3e.fandom.com/wiki/Exalted_3e_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-3e.fandom.com/wiki/Exalted_3e_Wiki</a><br /> <br /> Your points are disingenuous when they aren't outright incorrect.<br /> <br /> Blaque you made a similar point, but without the arrogant condescension. I don't know whether the Neverborn 'don't want anything' since they aren't really sentient and don't take direct action, but the fact of the matter is their existence tends to drive Creation toward non-existence. You will notice that I did not make sweeping statements about any of the categories, except the Neverborn. I acknowledge that individuals in all of the categories have differing motives, but that on the whole they each (with the exception of the Celestial Exalted) they tend to make mortal survival more in peril than they would be were these groups absent.<br /> <br /> I think that you have a point that I may be improperly carrying over my sense that the world is always doomed from 2e. You are correct that the world is less doomed than it was previously, and that I am filling gaps in my information with a highly negative possibility. But the setting does tend to fall apart if you think about it too hard, which is not necessarily a fatal criticism, many settings do this. Frankly, it's probably not an important critique what so ever so long as the setting enables you to tell compelling stories within the setting, which happily exalted does. (Please also note that in my original post this was a small aside that we have all apparently decided was the real point)<br /> <br /> But consider for a moment the United States government, the government of the most powerful nation on earth. There are about 2 million government employees for a population of about 300 million, and by most estimates, the government is woefully underfunded and understaffed. There are approximately 30,000 exalted in total, attempting to rule over 500 million mortals (give or take, many are in independent governments not associated with the realm or Lookshy) without the help of modern conveniences. Moreover, there are zero factions in the world, now or ever, that had human extinction as a major goal and yet we may still manage to kill ourselves off.<br /> <br /> As much as I disliked Levi's style of argument, he does make a good point that the Dragonblooded form institutions that amass and distribute power effectively. But that is only useful insofar as it is possible to amass enough power to plausibly fight back. Consider the possibility of a deathlord with Supernal Occult and sorcery, with Total Annihilation he could launch several nukes a day (with a bunch of restrictions, fair), and then raise them from the dead as his army for the next invasion. Point being that it doesn't require a ton of people want to destroy creation to cause serious damage to human life and make the setting nothing like its current status quo.<br /> <br /> There are also a ton of metaphysical questions that it raises. For instance, someone pointed out that the animals with essence abilities are because they are familiars, this is not universally true (or at least there are a large number of inexplicably animal-like magical creatures like Barrow Hounds, Gravehounds, aurochs, etc. Some magical beings, like the Cockatrice, are spontaneously magic offspring from non-magic animals). But to the extent it is true, it raises the similar question of why it is impossible for Solars to do the same to humans and awaken their innate magic, and if they don't have such magic, then why do animals? Moreover, why are ghosts more magical than humans? Some like the Susurrus makes sense since they are amalgamations of human souls and thus more 'powerful' in some indefinite manner. But others are merely dead people, yet now endowed with powers unavailable to them in life. Why are humans incapable of accessing this potential before death when so many other beings can?<br /> <br /> Now despite all the words I have typed, all of that is completely beside the point. I'm just apparently incapable of not arguing on the internet. The reason I am interested in collecting material for 'heroic mortals' is that I like the concept. I like the idea that with enough learning, training, or sheer determination a mortal can be a player in the universe without exalting and I like the idea of a wise old master who the players can learn from, despite being able to overpower. Its a staple of wuxia fiction, and even heroic myth. I also like the idea of having a power-tier somewhere between the exalted and the extra. If its not your cup of tea that's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","user":"Nabirius","date":". 02-07-2019, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T00:21:17-08:00","id":1285500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285499#post1285499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey Levi, are you always this much of a prick?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://exalted-3e.fandom.com/wiki/Exalted_3e_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-3e.fandom.com/wiki/Exalted_3e_Wiki</a><br /> <br /> Now kindly piss off. Your points are disingenuous when they aren't outright incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure when Isator said &quot;I don't think you are&quot; he meant &quot;I don't think you are missing anything&quot; not &quot;I don't think you are making a wiki&quot;, please calm down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8977-sigfriedmcwild","name":"sigfriedmcwild","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8977_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T00:28:48-08:00","id":1285501,"title":"","content":"That was the impression that I took away.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can see missing are certain artefacts, and there's blessings granted by Lunars. In 2e they could grant permanent mutations and instill immunity to fear. I don't know what they'll be able to do in 3e, but I'm sure it will be something.<br /> <br /> It's been mentioned that they'll be able to turn people into beastmen.<br /> <br /> I think mortals' best defence against the supernatural though, is going to be numbers, wards (salt, cold iron, etc) and prayers to local deities who can protect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T01:23:21-08:00","id":1285507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sigfriedmcwild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285500#post1285500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure when Isator said &quot;I don't think you are&quot; he meant &quot;I don't think you are missing anything&quot; not &quot;I don't think you are making a wiki&quot;, please calm down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that is what he meant I apologize, I misread his statement. Though frankly, I object to the overall hostile and condescending tone of his posts. However, if that was unintended or something that I read into the post, I again apologize. I am not intending to start flame wars.<br /> <br /> Oz, can mortals generally attune to artifacts, or does it have to be a specialized artifact? There was a powerful scepter in 2e that allowed mortals to wield it and create powerful laws, but I don't know how much of a feature this is in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","user":"Nabirius","date":". 02-07-2019, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T02:19:14-08:00","id":1285514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285507#post1285507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If that is what he meant I apologize, I misread his statement. Though frankly, I object to the overall hostile and condescending tone of his posts. However, if that was unintended or something that I read into the post, I again apologize. I am not intending to start flame wars.<br /> <br /> Oz, can mortals generally attune to artifacts, or does it have to be a specialized artifact? There was a powerful scepter in 2e that allowed mortals to wield it and create powerful laws, but I don't know how much of a feature this is in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect still has his staff and is still mortal. It\u2019s specific to the artifact however, not a general rule. Vainglory is an example from arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T02:23:04-08:00","id":1285515,"title":"","content":"The deathlords really aren't trying to wipe out Creation all that hard. Like yeah, they kill people, but generally that's to some other end. Like ghost armies, or soulsteel. <br /> <br /> I mean, up until Thorns nobody in creation really knew the deathlords were a thing. So clearly, they're not that active.<br /> <br /> The fair folk don't give a shit about destroying creation these days. Balor was cool, but he failed, the story is over. Nobody's gonna copy him. That'd be boring. <br /> <br /> Oh, also the Lunars have like, mortal populations they protect as well. And if a community is in trouble it's god might petition the sun for exigence. So it's not just the dragon blooded protecting everyone. If a community is seriously under threat, people have a habit of starting to glow. <br /> <br /> And you shouldn't discount what baseline mortals can manage. There are divinely sponsored mortal militia like the Brides of Ahlat, or the gunsosha, and I wouldn't assume these two were the only examples on the map. You got the lintha, who mostly want to nick your stuff but hey, can't steal from people if they're dead. <br /> <br /> And beastmen. Beastmen are not just a lunar thing. Yeah, they get charms to furry people up, but the way they used to do it? That's just a wyld thing now. Anyone can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T03:23:42-08:00","id":1285518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e#post1285472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As a side note, how do people feel about the loss of enlightened mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>My first real 2e Solar was designed from character creation to go around unlocking people's hidden power and teaching them Terrestrial Martial Arts, she had herself been an orphan raised by a crime syndicate who got the first real sense of control and purpose in her life from her martial arts. <br /> <br /> I honestly don't miss them.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Martial Art charms without combos or excellencies were mostly just <i>bad</i>. The charms simply weren't designed to be used solo in this fashion and most of them had effects that were contingent upon hitting the target in the first place, so there were obvious favourites and the rest were expensive speedbumps.<br /> <br /> There's also a lot of confirmation bias on the effectiveness of some styles because they revolved around enhancing tactics that were already way too good in 2nd edition to begin with but are remembered fondly because they were people's first experience of using them or because you could grudgingly respect these strategies from people who don't really have any other cards to play under the circumstances.<br /> <br /> Though I've come to realise there's a bit of a &quot;mortals don't matter&quot; sentiment in there, in that people who attempted more mundane approaches tended to get written off as extras even when they were doing something suicidal brave like fighting a Solar 5 vs 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T04:13:13-08:00","id":1285528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285518#post1285518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I've come to realise there's a bit of a &amp;quot;mortals don't matter&amp;quot; sentiment in there, in that people who attempted more mundane approaches tended to get written off as extras even when they were doing something suicidal brave like fighting a Solar 5 vs 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you mean by they don't matter because as a whole they are important to the setting. Even if they can't really win 1v1 against alnost anything with an essence pool. <br /> <br /> Also, enlightened humans wouldn't really change much. Enlightened humans only got acess to the weakest of charms or attuned an artifact that would be a what a 1/5th of their essence pool. Exalted is such a power heavy game that they'd still lose against a blood ape unless they managed to first turn 1 shot it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T07:28:44-08:00","id":1285558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285507#post1285507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oz, can mortals generally attune to artifacts, or does it have to be a specialized artifact? There was a powerful scepter in 2e that allowed mortals to wield it and create powerful laws, but I don't know how much of a feature this is in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of stuff like Yellow Jade or the Path of Technomantic Transcendance, or the Staff of the Perfect, yeah.<br /> <br /> In 3e there's Gunzosha Armour (as yet unstatted, it'll probably be in Heirs to the Shogunate) and Vainglory (a chakram in Arms you can attune for WP). And there's a few miscallaneous artefacts that just don't need to be attuned at all.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, the main way a mortal is going to get magical powers to challenge exalts and gods, is via sorcerous workings. Terrestrial workings can give someone mutations, while Celestial workings can give someone greater powers, like a hypnotic gaze or blood that turns into scorpions when shed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of a wise old master who the players can learn from, despite being able to overpower. Its a staple of wuxia fiction, and even heroic myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, in 3rd edition, you can do this with either mortal martial artists or sorcerers.<br /> <br /> An old mortal Mantis master can teach you Mantis style, right the way to the top. You'll be better than him of course, and could probably beat him up, but you learn the charms from him.<br /> <br /> Similarly with a mortal sorcerer, though only for Terrestrial Circle unfortunately. If you want to learn the ultimate secret techniques you'll need something more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a side note, how do people feel about the loss of enlightened mortals? </div> </div> </div>Mixed.<br /> On the one hand, it often seemed like you had a Solar (or whatever) going around powering up mortals in very boring ways so they could wield artefacts or whatever.<br /> There didn't really seem to be any actual enlightenment. Just a Solar grabbing a guy and buffing him permanently.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, enlightened martial artists were the default low-level antagonists for my friend's game, and it was very Wuxia. An enlightened Immaculate Monk using the first 5 charms of Five Dragon and a straight sword was the perfect Immaculate goon. Very genre-appropriate.<br /> <br /> Obviously, now you can have a mortal monk who actually practices Earth Dragon to help them become close to Pasiap. Or a local dojo that teaches Tiger Style (it was ridiculous how mortals in 2nd ed couldn't use Tiger Style when people in real life can).<br /> But the rules are pretty damn boring, in such a way that a soldier in armour with a spear is better; which is entirely realistic, but doesn't encourage the ST to run things in a genre-appropriate way.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the only way to have martial artists who stand out from soldiers is by making them Dragon-blooded, or maybe God-Blooded or something (which isn't necessarily going to make them better at martial arts). And if your game is all about kung-fu societies and stuff, it's going to get old fast. There aren't that many Exalts in Creation, after all.<br /> <br /> On the other other hand... as Lioness said, it was no good them having Martial Arts when they still couldn't actually hit anything. Some styles had charms to help with that; most didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-07-2019, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T07:30:18-08:00","id":1285560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285528#post1285528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, enlightened humans wouldn't really change much. Enlightened humans only got acess to the weakest of charms or attuned an artifact that would be a what a 1/5th of their essence pool. Exalted is such a power heavy game that they'd still lose against a blood ape unless they managed to first turn 1 shot it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much.<br /> <br /> Mostly, from what I saw, enlightened mortals were basically either low-level combatants (which is okay) or Solar followers as part of some scheme to mass produce thaumaturgy or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T07:37:04-08:00","id":1285561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285499#post1285499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey Levi, there is literally no reason for your hostility and condescension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Sorry. I'll try better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your points are disingenuous when they aren't outright incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... how?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">they tend to make mortal survival more in peril than they would be were these groups absent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of my points before were that mortals are not in enough peril to widely knock down their population. Enough to slow down worldwide population growth, but not knock the overall down.<br /> <br /> In places where population density is low, it can be hard to effectively find people, and even when you do the yields are low. In places where density is high, they're probably the best protected by their labours providing fortifications, numbers providing armies, and attracting or clustering around supernatural protectors.<br /> <br /> Some of my other points have been about pointing to ways in which mortal life being in continuous peril is a thing that can go on for ages without killing absolutely everybody, for the sake of getting one to consider what that kind of world must be like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Please also note that in my original post this was a small aside that we have all apparently decided was the real point)</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that one doesn't see how mortals survive is a rather weighted question, and when it's linked to the topic of them getting supernatural powers, it would kind of shape the priorities if taken as a given.<br /> <br /> I think that it's a net positive to devising the powers that they can get if the survival of humanity is not dependent on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, there are zero factions in the world, now or ever, that had human extinction as a major goal and yet we may still manage to kill ourselves off.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a lot of those are things that aren't really in the game setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider the possibility of a deathlord with Supernal Occult and sorcery, with Total Annihilation he could launch several nukes a day (with a bunch of restrictions, fair), and then raise them from the dead as his army for the next invasion. Point being that it doesn't require a ton of people want to destroy creation to cause serious damage to human life and make the setting nothing like its current status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Deathlords will have Supernal or Chtonic Abilities (not that it necessarily matters if none of them are below Essence 5 anyway), and they might not be able to use Solar Sorcery.<br /> <br /> A few of them might still have highly formidable powers, but going forwards, Deathlords ought to have certain restrictions arising from their ghostly natures. For the sake of consistency in the setting, an incentive to have the Abyssals, and making them feel more like ancient ghosts overall.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I initially thought to make the &quot;humans with magic&quot; side a separate post, but... it wouldn't be so long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, someone pointed out that the animals with essence abilities are because they are familiars, this is not universally true (or at least there are a large number of inexplicably animal-like magical creatures like Barrow Hounds, Gravehounds, aurochs, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are aurochs magical? Regardless, the other things... calling these entities being animal-like inexplicable begs the question of what one would presume a supernatural entity to be like, and why.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, when talking about something like the cockatrice... regardless of the in-setting specifics of how they exist, I can see the question of &quot;why don't such spontaneous blessings or curses, from the Wyld or whatever other source, come upon humans more&quot;.<br /> <br /> I can think of three avenues for that.<br /> <br /> One is that such a thing is generally how thaumaturges happen. Thaumaturges might be meant to be uncommon on the whole, but even assuming that the odds were something fairly remote like 1 in 10,000, across the whole world that still amounts to... fifty thousand people.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that's a bit low for me...shorten the odds a bit.<br /> <br /> The circumstances that create the likes of cockatrices aren't exactly common, especially when people are vigilant against them.<br /> <br /> Wait, I said three... damned rambling.<br /> <br /> Human behaviour might be less susceptible to things like spontaneous Wyld emergences, and the background of the setting has often made humans specifically, even deliberately, non-magical, which might also preclude a lot of weird stuff happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">why it is impossible for Solars to do the same to humans and awaken their innate magic</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving aside innate magic, I'd say that Solars can bestow power in a manner consistent with the Solar way of doing things. Look at how they can train soldiers to have Might when fighting spirits or giant monsters. Barring sorcery, a Solar's training or blessings aren't going to make another Eternal Revolutionary, because that doesn't fit the image of their power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if they don't have such magic, then why do animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>A cockatrice doesn't happen because chickens are innately magical, they happen because the Wyld seeps in to weird happenstance.<br /> <br /> A similar logic probably goes for any instance where a more magical creature has been transformed; that Death Essence isn't awakening their latent potential, they're just a thematically suitable vessel for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, why are ghosts more magical than humans? Some like the Susurrus makes sense since they are amalgamations of human souls and thus more 'powerful' in some indefinite manner. But others are merely dead people, yet now endowed with powers unavailable to them in life. Why are humans incapable of accessing this potential before death when so many other beings can?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of two ways to go with this.<br /> <br /> One is that, in life, that energy goes into fuelling your living self; sustaining your body, your intellect, your passions. Being separated from mortal flesh frees a lot of that energy to be bent to other purposes, but at the cost of losing Life; warmth, sensation, newness, strong emotion.<br /> <br /> The other is that ghost powers rise from channeling the Underworld's Essence, which generally can't be done by the living. Maybe sometimes, but those origins might not be pleasant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that with enough learning, training, or sheer determination a mortal can be a player in the universe without exalting</div> </div> </div> </div>It needs to compromise a bit with the existing setting, but it's perfectly doable. It's often becoming a sorcerer, but can be other things.<br /> <br /> Artifact backstory in Arms and What Fire Has Wrought often mention conflicts against people that weren't Exalted, but still utilising some form of power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of a wise old master who the players can learn from, despite being able to overpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's something that a character can be without having any powers at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T08:02:39-08:00","id":1285566,"title":"","content":"The impression I got is that enlightened mortals didn't really help with the issue of mortals being weak; they just lowered the bar a little. Enlightenment was a &quot;You're magical enough to matter&quot; badge for a mortal. Just enough magic to be relevant in a system that ignored everything non-magical and a patch-job on the underlying issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T08:16:12-08:00","id":1285569,"title":"","content":"That's fair. They were still very weak compared to an Exalt.<br /> <br /> Though an-old-man-who-definitely-wasn't-the-Perfect did beat several of our PCs in a kung-fu tournament. Obviously no one wanted to flare, so they couldn't use most of their power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T08:24:56-08:00","id":1285572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Consider the possibility of a deathlord with Supernal Occult and sorcery, with Total Annihilation he could launch several nukes a day (with a bunch of restrictions, fair),</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather not. It breaks the game, because Deathlords with a desire to destroy the world and Total Annihlation really doesn't make much sense in a setting which seems notably devoid of Deathlords casting Total Annihlation everywhere.<br /> (Also, Supernal Occult doesn't help you get Sorcery anyway. And also they all have higher essence than 5. 5 is for Nephwracks. Even in 2nd ed, the lowest Essence they had was 7, and some had 10.)<br /> <br /> Deathlords (well, at least 1) with a desire to destroy the world and the Great Contagion does make sense, but it's the only super-weapon that does make sense for them to have (as it's the only one they've used). Unless you can think of some other thing to stop them, of course. But there has to be some explanation of why (except for the Great Contagion) Deathlords haven't been running around throwing superweapons everywhere. &quot;They can't do that&quot; is the easiest, of course.<br /> <br /> Clearly, from the setting's history, this isn't something that mortals have really had to worry about for about 800 years ago. Same with the Fair Folk's desire to destroy Creation.<br /> <br /> I mean, they do have to deal with Hungry Ghosts, marauding Hobgoblins (near the edge of Creation, not close to the Blessed Isle of course), the occasional escaped demon, etc. But those are things that a lot of mortals working together, with wards of some kind, can to some extent deal with.<br /> <br /> (I don't want to say too much more on this, as I recognise this was just a tangent, and not actually the main point of this thread.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:24:23-08:00","id":1285633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285566#post1285566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impression I got is that enlightened mortals didn't really help with the issue of mortals being weak; they just lowered the bar a little. Enlightenment was a &quot;You're magical enough to matter&quot; badge for a mortal. Just enough magic to be relevant in a system that ignored everything non-magical and a patch-job on the underlying issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also to some extent martial arts styles can provide the basis of a memorable aesthetic by restricting characters to equipment that's stylistic and non-optimal. <br /> Sometimes the true power of a terrestrial martial artist was that they required a modicum of descriptive effort from the Storyteller saying what they were armed with and dressed like helped senpai notice them. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:38:11-08:00","id":1285670,"title":"","content":"That was certainly my experience, though that might simply be because my ST was always more interested in unusual societies of martial artists and their philosophies than in soldiers or bandits.<br /> (But then, they are more interesting. And part of the genre of Exalted.)<br /> <br /> I guess that, when 3rd ed was written, this was supposed to continue via Techniques, so as to still keep the aesthetic of all the Martial Artists running around Creation having duels and learning at dojos, and so on.<br /> Unfortunately, they never managed to crack that for balance reasons, so it ended up with mortal martial artists just not being very well supported.*<br /> <br /> *In the sense that they're just a bit weak compared to a soldier in chainmail with a shield and short sword. Accurate, but not genre-appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T14:00:31-08:00","id":1285677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285670#post1285670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was certainly my experience, though that might simply be because my ST was always more interested in unusual societies of martial artists and their philosophies than in soldiers or bandits.<br /> (But then, they are more interesting. And part of the genre of Exalted.)<br /> <br /> I guess that, when 3rd ed was written, this was supposed to continue via Techniques, so as to still keep the aesthetic of all the Martial Artists running around Creation having duels and learning at dojos, and so on.<br /> Unfortunately, they never managed to crack that for balance reasons, so it ended up with mortal martial artists just not being very well supported.*<br /> <br /> *In the sense that they're just a bit weak compared to a soldier in chainmail with a shield and short sword. Accurate, but not genre-appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will note, though, that due to 3e's general defaulting to Quick Characters, it's not htat hard to just make the martial artist NPC good at being a badass mortal martial artist via the QC rules. I think that a bit of the view that there's something lacking in Martial Arts mechancially in 3e is built on the idea that NPCs should be using the same mechanics as PCs for character creation and equipment implementation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T14:05:23-08:00","id":1285682,"title":"","content":"Eh, I think it's a bit difficult to justify a mortal martial artist having a Soak of 10 like an Elite Soldier in his armour does.<br /> (Obviously you can have all the other stats of a mortal soldier. You always could. No rules are needed for that particularly.)<br /> <br /> I could say &quot;he practices being stabbed in the head every day so now his skin is hard as rubble&quot; but then the PCs are going to be all &quot;why can't I do that?&quot; And I'll say &quot;you can, if you learn a charm.&quot; And they'll say &quot;so he's using a charm? Mortals can't use charms!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T14:39:31-08:00","id":1285693,"title":"","content":"Generally I just think that characters have the statst hey need. If you're not wanting to give the martial artist the higher Soak, just give them a higher Dodge Deefense. Give them some special unique Merits that represent their understanding of the secrets fo the style that PCs fully unlock with Charms. Basically a way to do &quot;mortal martial arts&quot; often to me is just...give them Merits that do some semblance fo what the Charm probably does. Because the Charms basically are just pulling that weight and there's no need for QCs to follow the rules so strictly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T15:11:07-08:00","id":1285700,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but if I give them Evasion 7, is that not kind of weird?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T18:29:51-08:00","id":1285758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285700#post1285700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but if I give them Evasion 7, is that not kind of weird?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it be? QCs should be designed to be interesting challenges to PCs and express their role in a story well. Their stats reflect their narrative importance, not some statement of their actual relative power or traits in the world as some measure of their real traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T01:26:28-08:00","id":1285828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285481#post1285481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and there's not a single one of them, in 3E, who can't be pulled off their horse and murdered by a sufficient number of determined mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Except the Lunars, because Legendary Size makes you nigh-impervious to battle groups. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T03:22:09-08:00","id":1285840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285828#post1285828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Except the Lunars, because Legendary Size makes you nigh-impervious to battle groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pity the horse that has to carry a Lunar who's wearing an ox-dragon's shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T06:28:35-08:00","id":1285870,"title":"","content":"Don't pity the horse.<br /> She was the Lunar all along.<br /> The rider who died was just one of her clones. Like a worm who leaves behind its tail to fool predators into thinking they'd eaten it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why would it be? QCs should be designed to be interesting challenges to PCs and express their role in a story well. Their stats reflect their narrative importance, not some statement of their actual relative power or traits in the world as some measure of their real traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of agree with you, and kind of not.<br /> <br /> I'm quite happy for a Solar QC to have charms that don't actually work the same as ones in the charms section of the Core, for the sake of simplicity and power (Solar charms are designed to work in aggregate, but as ST I don't have time to assign and remember 30 charms for every Solar NPC). For example, I don't care if they have one Melee charm which is just &quot;double 8s&quot; or something, rather than the first 5 melee charms of the Solar Melee tree.<br /> <br /> But not of course, if they're charms like &quot;you shoot fire from your eyes&quot; or &quot;you summon an army made of sunlight&quot; because those aren't things Solars can actually do.<br /> <br /> Abilities/attributes do represent something. There's a whole chapter on that. A person with Dexterity and Melee 5, and a Specialty in swords, is explicitly one of the 5 greatest mortal swordsman in the entirety of Creation. And the greatest swordsmen in all of Creation have Parry ([5+5+1]/2+1)=7.<br /> <br /> So if the PCs run into a hot-shot mortal immaculate who fights with a staff and has Parry 8, they're going to ask &quot;wtf&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> But that isn't actually the point I was making.<br /> <br /> The question is, &quot;why, fluff-wise, is the practicioner of an esoteric and bizarre unarmoured and unarmed fighting style just as good as a professional soldier?&quot;<br /> Now, in real life, the answer is &quot;they're not.&quot;<br /> And in Exalted, when talking about mortals, they're also not.<br /> Even if they have the same stats, the soldier is better because she has armour and a better Parry (because of a medium weapon).<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, the answer was &quot;actually, the practicioner of an esoteric and bizarre unarmoured and unarmed fighting style has unlocked the secrets of Qi, so can rival or even beat a soldier.&quot;<br /> Which isn't realistic, but it is appropriate for the genre.<br /> <br /> If your answer is &quot;just give the Martial Artist higher Defence&quot;, well, why can't the soldier have that? Why does the Martial Artist get better stats?<br /> In 2nd ed, kung-fu was magic. In 3rd ed, it's not. It just allows people who are already magic to use a wider variety of magic.<br /> <br /> Now, there are some game balance reasons for this, of course. And in terms of Exalts, I think it works fine.<br /> But that's why I said I did miss enlightened mortals a bit. Not enlightened sorcerer-engineers or thaumaturgists, but enlightened martial artists.<br /> <br /> Now, the only people who can really power up via kung-fu enlightenment is Dragonblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T07:13:13-08:00","id":1285877,"title":"","content":"Wait, what happens when a sixth person gets five dots in Dexterity, five dots in Melee, and a specialty in Swords? Does one of the previous five spontaneously die of heart failure?<br /> <br /> I would think that being ranked among the top 5 swordsmen in the world would by necessity involve <i>competing</i> in some fashion. Though I guess it could be one of those <i>The Highlander</i>-type situations, where people who acquire the necessary dots just find themselves drawn inexplicably to do battle with the other dot-holders, culling the numbers down until only five are left.<br /> <br /> Still, &quot;There can be only five\u2026&quot; it's just not quite as catchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-08-2019, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T07:20:24-08:00","id":1285881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285870#post1285870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, &quot;why, fluff-wise, is the practicioner of an esoteric and bizarre unarmoured and unarmed fighting style just as good as a professional soldier?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought it was about Immaculate Monks until this point and wondered why you insisted on castrating their effectiveness by restricting them to fighting barehanded in stereotypical monk garb. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T09:07:08-08:00","id":1285922,"title":"","content":"I run strictly-mortal campaigns in 3E, and so long as the mortals are well developed and intelligent, they can stand up to many things.<br /> <br /> A farmer that has never held a spear in his life organized into a poorly-led mob? Yeah, no, sausage for the grinder for the 3 seconds they decide to stand and fight<br /> <br /> A well-led, well-motivated, well-trained and well-equipped mortal can kill plenty of shite.<br /> <br /> My players have killed ghosts, demons, Fae, monstrous animals, armies, and even a few Exalts. Even a Prince of the Earth wont survive a pike through the heart, much less 6.<br /> <br /> Most non-intelligent beasts and monsters would prefer to avoid injury, and can be driven off if a potential target is enough of a PITA. My mortal players organized a village to drive off a hungry Tyrant Lizard by slinging stones at it and poking it with long sticks until it fucked off in search of easier prey.<br /> <br /> Most intelligent &quot;monsters&quot; can be bargained with.<br /> <br /> Finally, even with all of the monsters and madmen and supernatural shite Creation has on display, the most common problems a mortal settlement is likely to deal with is wolves (or some other predator) taking their livestock and bandits shaking them down for goods and deterring away traders. Both can be dealt with with a little steel-in-the-spine and steel-in-the-hand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T09:24:26-08:00","id":1285926,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m actually kind of curious now, has anyone run like 4-5 combat focused mortals against a tyrant lizard? It\u2019s been too long since I\u2019ve played to intuit from stats alone, but I imagine if all involved had reatively heavy weapons and armor it might work out? Like even a fight to the death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T11:39:09-08:00","id":1285967,"title":"","content":"Presumably you also want to poison your weapons, since IIRC only Exalts and magical creatures can reduce poison to 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T11:43:57-08:00","id":1285969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285870#post1285870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's why I said I did miss enlightened mortals a bit. Not enlightened sorcerer-engineers or thaumaturgists, but enlightened martial artists.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it happens, I've been working on a few ideas for mortal characters (aiming at putting something up on the Storyteller's Vault), and this is one of the things I'm looking to capture. My current approach is to allow mortals to follow a specific code of conduct (I'm developing several examples) to earn &quot;Enlightenment XP&quot; (by analogy with Solar or Dragon XP for filling character roles or playing the limitations for Flaws). But rather than being used to buy Charms or abilities or the like, Enlightenment XP can be cashed in for motes to power MA charms.<br /> <br /> So, for example, a PC mortal MA following the Path of Temperance can earn Enlightenment XP for being restricted by her ascetic principles in play, thus gaining a pool of points that can be expended to power her bought-with-ordinary-experience Golden Janissary Style charms. Obviously, that means she'll have to husband use of those charms in ways characters with actual mote pools don't, but when the situation merits it, she can use her &quot;secret technique&quot; of Golden Janissary Form to kick ass.<br /> <br /> (So far, my rough-draft paths are Temperance, Compassion, Valor, Filial Piety, and Blood Sacrifice. The Immaculate Order strongly favors Temperance; Compassion is uncommon and often considered socially subversive; Valor is popular among those who focus on martial glory; Filial Piety is most common in places with strong ancestor cults; and Blood Sacrifice is popularly associated with Yozi cults and Anathema and seen as &quot;cheating the system&quot; by followers of other paths.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T13:30:44-08:00","id":1286001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285969#post1285969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As it happens, I've been working on a few ideas for mortal characters (aiming at putting something up on the Storyteller's Vault), and this is one of the things I'm looking to capture. My current approach is to allow mortals to follow a specific code of conduct (I'm developing several examples) to earn &quot;Enlightenment XP&quot; (by analogy with Solar or Dragon XP for filling character roles or playing the limitations for Flaws). But rather than being used to buy Charms or abilities or the like, Enlightenment XP can be cashed in for motes to power MA charms.<br /> <br /> So, for example, a PC mortal MA following the Path of Temperance can earn Enlightenment XP for being restricted by her ascetic principles in play, thus gaining a pool of points that can be expended to power her bought-with-ordinary-experience Golden Janissary Style charms. Obviously, that means she'll have to husband use of those charms in ways characters with actual mote pools don't, but when the situation merits it, she can use her &quot;secret technique&quot; of Golden Janissary Form to kick ass.<br /> <br /> (So far, my rough-draft paths are Temperance, Compassion, Valor, Filial Piety, and Blood Sacrifice. The Immaculate Order strongly favors Temperance; Compassion is uncommon and often considered socially subversive; Valor is popular among those who focus on martial glory; Filial Piety is most common in places with strong ancestor cults; and Blood Sacrifice is popularly associated with Yozi cults and Anathema and seen as &quot;cheating the system&quot; by followers of other paths.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like that way of dealing with that, and will probably be stealing that (or something similar) for my games. I'll have to keep my eye out for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T20:38:43-08:00","id":1286083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285870#post1285870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Abilities/attributes do represent something. There's a whole chapter on that. A person with Dexterity and Melee 5, and a Specialty in swords, is explicitly one of the 5 greatest mortal swordsman in the entirety of Creation. And the greatest swordsmen in all of Creation have Parry ([5+5+1]/2+1)=7.</div> </div> </div> </div>QCs don't have Attributes and Abilities. Their pool caps are baed on them, but simply put, a person hast hose stats because that is what's approrpiate to the character for the role they have in a story. The Defense 7 isn't hiding some actaul stat. THey have Defense 7 because that's what the character needed to be interesting in teh role they needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285870#post1285870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, &quot;why, fluff-wise, is the practicioner of an esoteric and bizarre unarmoured and unarmed fighting style just as good as a professional soldier?&quot;<br /> Now, in real life, the answer is &quot;they're not.&quot;<br /> And in Exalted, when talking about mortals, they're also not.<br /> Even if they have the same stats, the soldier is better because she has armour and a better Parry (because of a medium weapon).</div> </div> </div> </div>They have it because that's what they needed for the stats. QCs aren't &quot;Really trait X+Y&quot; to me. They're just the traits they have. The martial artist with Defense 7 is probably among the best in the world. What that &quot;really is in stats&quot; Is irreelvant, as the only stat that exists for them is Defense 7. &quot;In real life&quot; doesn't matter, as the dice pools don't represent some mechancial sense of who he is objectively, just what they are narratively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285870#post1285870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your answer is &quot;just give the Martial Artist higher Defence&quot;, well, why can't the soldier have that? Why does the Martial Artist get better stats?<br /> In 2nd ed, kung-fu was magic. In 3rd ed, it's not. It just allows people who are already magic to use a wider variety of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The martial artist gets better stats because that's their narrative role. The rules aren't some engine to show what folks are in power to be fair. <i>No stats exist besides the QC block</i>. To take it even further, the previous and current devs are even of an opinion that at this point, they probably should have just gone whole hog on that and not fully stat out any NPCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285870#post1285870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, there are some game balance reasons for this, of course. And in terms of Exalts, I think it works fine.<br /> But that's why I said I did miss enlightened mortals a bit. Not enlightened sorcerer-engineers or thaumaturgists, but enlightened martial artists.<br /> <br /> Now, the only people who can really power up via kung-fu enlightenment is Dragonblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you really, for sure must have it is probably something that can just be a unique Merit that gives them the better stat. That's the big thing to me. There doesn't need to be some architecture for mortals ot use shitty Charms so they feel special (but still ultimately pointless). If you want them to be equilvant to a soldier, just give htemt he stats and say they're better because their Martial Arts training gave them Merits that more or less get the job done. And if the Snake stylist player wants that shit, well, tough shit. They get Charms to do that and more.<br /> <br /> I guess to me, the big thing is that I kind fo fully embrace that there's not meant to be PC-QC symmetry on things like this. The martial artist isn't better than the soldier. She just has the stats needed to fulfill the role, which put her stats on par with said solider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T02:38:47-08:00","id":1286126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285870#post1285870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your answer is &quot;just give the Martial Artist higher Defence&quot;, well, why can't the soldier have that? Why does the Martial Artist get better stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason why the enlightened martial artist who knew a TMA up to the form had about 80xp worth of upgrades on the soldier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T02:48:46-08:00","id":1286132,"title":"","content":"Yes, but I mean there was a setting reason before; kung fu is magic. And the mechanics reflected that in some way (it doesn't precisely matter how).<br /> <br /> Now, kung-fu does not seem to be magic (or rather, it contains secret magic that can only be unlocked by magical superhumans. But only by magical superhumans). It's just... kung fu. But that doesn't reflect the genre.<br /> <br /> I don't really care about how one mechanically reflects that, and if the answer is &quot;kung-fu mastery gives mortals Defence 7&quot;, sure (I mean, that seems a very boring way to do it, but okay). But the game ought to say &quot;mortals can use kung fu to attain mastery of combat in a way that normal combat training does not&quot; if that's what we're going with, and it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Whereas in 2nd ed it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T03:44:11-08:00","id":1286139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286132#post1286132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but I mean there was a setting reason before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue there still is.<br /> The assertion with that mismatch is that the martial artist and the soldier could've walked similar paths but the former has put more so much more work into this while the latter depends on fighting as part of a unit and the quality of their equipment. It's just that this also works out as being more of a protagonist than the other guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T04:32:46-08:00","id":1286141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286132#post1286132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, kung-fu does not seem to be magic (or rather, it contains secret magic that can only be unlocked by magical superhumans. But only by magical superhumans). It's just... kung fu. But that doesn't reflect the genre.</div> </div> </div> </div>We got the lady with a soul snake from her secret snake school. Pretty sure kung fu still does magic, just not uniformly and not always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T04:59:05-08:00","id":1286145,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I didn't know that.<br /> I just saw that it was another mortal, like the spy or the barbarian, and didn't buy it (I can make mortals myself). I just went and bought it now.<br /> That's pretty cool, I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T06:11:53-08:00","id":1286162,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a>, these questions do seem to come down to both a genre or setting side to it, and an implementation side of it. <br /> <br /> My perception is it sort of comes back to that idea, which actually Exalted has been somewhat inconsistent on, of how much mortals and Exalted are in a separate kind of action genre. In one corner, mortals in a brutally realistic mode and the Exalted's power is to make stylish, fanciful wuxia/Hong Kong action cinema stuff happen. In that mode, fancy techniques don't really give you as much edge as cunning or a sharp blade, and mortal MA not really having an edge is a feature, not bug. Mortals live in Yoji Yamada's samurai trilogy and Exalts live in Ninja Scroll or Samurai Shodown or Kenshin land. Or alternatively, if they're actually both in that same stylish action genre with those tropes where they can become badass through kung fu and the Exalted are just stronger and can do more blatantly supernatural stuff.<br /> <br /> So that's a genre question, then separately there's the implementation of whether TMA using mortals is a good way to do mortals who've become powerful through kung fu.... or actually it's mechanically an overweight way to do what can be abstracted out and implemented through ad hoc bonuses on QCs, since most of these mortals are not going to actually be player characters.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that QCs generally imply setting 'facts' (if that's a reasonable at all summary of the gist of your comments). Like if you commonly build Godblooded QC in your games who can fight a Solar on an even level despite not being particularly old or experienced or special, that implies 'facts' about the world, rather than being without implication just for the sake of story and good fights working out! QCs as a mechanical abstraction to reduce weight on the ST side, not an ability to abandon setting 'facts' (for want of a better term).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T13:52:13-08:00","id":1286283,"title":"","content":"I mean, another thing to remember is that in 3e, it's not the Martial Arts dots that give you magic. A way I think of it is that just knowing Snake Sytle doesn't give you shit besides dots in Snake Style and the ability to use cool weapons. But that you're a master of Snake Style probably opens up options storywise to other things, such as weird unique techniques (Meirts) or patronage for useful beings (as the characte rin Adversaries of the Righteous).<br /> <br /> I think that's the big thing to me. Even if it's a setting fact, that fact is not going to be realized by the Martial Arts Ablity all on its own giving out free beeenies. It is just a justificaiton for other things for a character, who is exceptional to get the Dodge 7.<br /> <br /> Mind, I also <i>don't</i> think the mechanics are setting facts, and that traits should be tailored to your grolup and the same character need not have the same numerical expression in every game, as what that means might be contextual to what your group does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T01:40:38-08:00","id":1286644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1285969#post1285969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As it happens, I've been working on a few ideas for mortal characters (aiming at putting something up on the Storyteller's Vault), and this is one of the things I'm looking to capture. My current approach is to allow mortals to follow a specific code of conduct (I'm developing several examples) to earn &quot;Enlightenment XP&quot; (by analogy with Solar or Dragon XP for filling character roles or playing the limitations for Flaws). But rather than being used to buy Charms or abilities or the like, Enlightenment XP can be cashed in for motes to power MA charms.<br /> <br /> So, for example, a PC mortal MA following the Path of Temperance can earn Enlightenment XP for being restricted by her ascetic principles in play, thus gaining a pool of points that can be expended to power her bought-with-ordinary-experience Golden Janissary Style charms. Obviously, that means she'll have to husband use of those charms in ways characters with actual mote pools don't, but when the situation merits it, she can use her &quot;secret technique&quot; of Golden Janissary Form to kick ass.<br /> <br /> (So far, my rough-draft paths are Temperance, Compassion, Valor, Filial Piety, and Blood Sacrifice. The Immaculate Order strongly favors Temperance; Compassion is uncommon and often considered socially subversive; Valor is popular among those who focus on martial glory; Filial Piety is most common in places with strong ancestor cults; and Blood Sacrifice is popularly associated with Yozi cults and Anathema and seen as &quot;cheating the system&quot; by followers of other paths.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that this works for my purposes exactly, but I really wanted to let you know that this is super fucking cool! If you have the document, would you mind posting it?<br /> <br /> I think Blaque has some excellent points about how QC characters don't really need to necessarily be obviously supernatural in order to make the game work and also have mechanical flavor. A martial artist or soldier might have parry 7 in the fight because in the narrative they are incredibly motivated as well as skilled, or are willing to take the kind of risks someone fighting with the expectation of surviving would not. Furthermore, merit or even made up techniques can certainly fill in for a charm tree.<br /> <br /> However, I do like playing mortal characters and running mortal campaigns, which are anime-esque but are on a lower power level and social status from the exalted. One of the reasons I haven't for 3e is that the linear warriors/quadratic wizards problem is truly gigantic here, a mortal sorcerer can do an enormous number of powerful effects even when limited to terrestrial workings and spells (bind a few 1st circle demons and go to town). My players are nicer than that, and I know the person who likes to play caster characters would play support, but there's no getting around how much more he brings to the table than the others. <br /> <br /> In those cases, I suppose there is nothing stopping me from just porting over the setting details from 2e which allowed for mortals to take terrestrial martial arts and open them up for unexalted mortals as well, but this is clearly a house rule and one that is kind of janky without a bunch of essence 3 mortals running around. I suspect part of this has to do with the fact that I agree with Oz that mortal magic martial arts are a good fit for the setting, its hard to see how the wise master can teach the solar things he is not mechanically capable of himself. <br /> <br /> I will say that I agree that enlightenment was too easy in the past, with solars being able to create enlighted shock troops in a matter of days. I think such enlightenment should be rather rare, possibly as rare as the exalted but requiring incredible devotion and discipline, much like how enlightened sorcery is implied to be a rare feat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","user":"Nabirius","date":". 02-11-2019, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T04:33:49-08:00","id":1286663,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the only kind of empowered mortal that's really gone is the &quot;I spent 5 years meditating and pulled myself up by my bootstraps&quot; kind.<br /> <br /> In 2e terms, Mist the Eternal Revolutionary is a guy who went Power Questing in the Wyld and Ku Nenavaya got an endowment from a Deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T06:52:35-08:00","id":1286688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286663#post1286663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the only kind of empowered mortal that's really gone is the &amp;quot;I spent 5 years meditating and pulled myself up by my bootstraps&amp;quot; kind.<br /> <br /> In 2e terms, Mist the Eternal Revolutionary is a guy who went Power Questing in the Wyld and Ku Nenavaya got an endowment from a Deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if you could even really say that the bootstraps kind is gone either then. They might just be as much of an oddity as the other kinds now, but not gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T07:09:58-08:00","id":1286695,"title":"","content":"&quot;So what's this guy's story?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He kung fu'd so hard he learned to use essence&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not sure you can do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you gonna tell <i>him</i> that?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T07:27:04-08:00","id":1286701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286688#post1286688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if you could even really say that the bootstraps kind is gone either then. They might just be as much of an oddity as the other kinds now, but not gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any kind of canon ninja will stop you from writing them in your game, but they're probably not going to appear in published materials, whereas others like Mist and Ku Nenayeva have and will continue to appear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":23657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","user":"VioletDreamer","date":". 02-11-2019, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T01:16:59-08:00","id":1286994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286644#post1286644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that this works for my purposes exactly, but I really wanted to let you know that this is super fucking cool! If you have the document, would you mind posting it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still working on it as part of the intended larger <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?filters=0_45735_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Vault</a> work, which is currently planned to also include 1) a lot of additional 3e thaumaturgy, 2) uses for Craft (Artifact) and Craft (Geomancy) for people who can't use Essence (and pointing out the current Craft rules seem to allow mortals to repair manses, just not build them), 3) expanded material for characters empowered by Prophet-Uplifting Evocation, 4) heavily-modified Dragon-Blooded and Lunar approximations of Prophet-Uplifting Evocation and their own expanded material, 5) ideas for dealing with mortal shamans/priests/chosen ones without thaumaturgy (noting the corebook gives a special ritual to a Bride of Ahlat on p.498), and 6) a few minor sidebars on other issues as ideas come to me (like what honest mortal non-thaumaturge astrology can say by looking at the stars, which is more than nothing but still very limited, on the level of fates of nations rather than personal romance, and how it's more accurate the better your telescope is because you can see fainter stars and more subtle changes and . . .).<br /> <br /> If the creation of the larger work falls through, I'll probably dump all my notes into a PDF, stick it on my web server, and point people at them. But my goal is a resource for all slightly-superhuman mortals, up where people browsing Exalted products can see it. (And my lunatic hope is to see the Storyteller Vault clause about the line adopting and canonizing community work invoked . . .)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286644#post1286644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that I agree that enlightenment was too easy in the past, with solars being able to create enlighted shock troops in a matter of days. I think such enlightenment should be rather rare, possibly as rare as the exalted but requiring incredible devotion and discipline, much like how enlightened sorcery is implied to be a rare feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e, of course, originally presented a five-years-of-asceticism thaumaturgical ritual for becoming an Enlightened mortal, which got me thinking about asceticism-powers-your-kung-fu. One thing that annoyed me about that is how someone could immediately abandon the asceticism after getting the essence pool, giving me the idea that you would have to instead <i>continually</i> adhere to it to recharge you pool. Then I saw how similar that was to the way flaws work in 3e (noting as an incidental bonus that using it as a flaw means that Exalted characters could then use the same code to earn their Solar/Dragon/Lunar/Whatever XP [mechanically justifying the &quot;your essence will be more refined if you adhere to ascetic discipline&quot; idea in a subtle, non-unbalancing way]). Followed by noticing that a flaw approach would support other character types following different ethical ideals, and poking at the 2e Virtue list and then reading some sources about Confucian and Roman ethics.<br /> <br /> Whether it all really works in play I can't say yet, but I love the whole interrelated mechanics-and-setting structure in my mind, down to your mortal supernatural martial artists only going nova when it's important because it takes them time to build it back up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T01:28:49-08:00","id":1286995,"title":"","content":"By the way, I realize that the current devs are opposed, but I personally think it should be fine for Prophet-Uplifting Evocation to allow mortals to learn and use MA charms &quot;normally&quot;. The strictly-limited numbers upliftable established in the charm avoid 2e Enlightened Mortal Factory concerns well enough, I feel. (My DB version is even stricter, allowing just <i>one</i> person to be &quot;folded in the dragon's wings&quot; by a DB, and that subject to several limits.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T01:56:04-08:00","id":1286999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286663#post1286663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the only kind of empowered mortal that's really gone is the &amp;quot;I spent 5 years meditating and pulled myself up by my bootstraps&amp;quot; kind.<br /> <br /> In 2e terms, Mist the Eternal Revolutionary is a guy who went Power Questing in the Wyld and Ku Nenavaya got an endowment from a Deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, depending on how many potential sorcerers one thinks there are in the world, it's always possible to get a form of enlightenment constituting an initiation, which frankly includes powers through Merits that are more impressive and interesting than what Second Edition mortals generally had.<br /> <br /> That was always my problem with the old Enlightened Essence, how boring it was. It didn't indicate anything, it didn't convey anything. The only thing worthwhile about it was what some people projected for the sake of Solar nation building schemes, and even those didn't often have much going for them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Let's give everybody a mote pool so they can do the thing where spending motes let's you skip the ritual and material requirements of thaumaturgy.&quot;<br /> &quot;So they can do all of the varied and weird cultural idiosyncracy stuff?&quot;<br /> &quot;Ew, no. Just gimme the generic Artifact maintenance rituals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell, I believe it was Eric who explicitly said that the next dedicated setting book is going to include rules for mortal magic ala the Linowan masks. That stuff is still going to exist, just not under the term and system of thaumaturgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T02:05:03-08:00","id":1287001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286688#post1286688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if you could even really say that the bootstraps kind is gone either then. They might just be as much of an oddity as the other kinds now, but not gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing inherently wrong with it, but fans of the bootstraps tend to not be keen on the idea that there's some special factor at play in how their character gained their abilities when others didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T08:53:09-08:00","id":1287549,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of facing this problem right now, as it happens. Some people have expressed interest in a Lunar game by me, once we have the full text. And while I'd like to pit them against the Guild, rather than the Realm... I kind of do worry they'd just steamroll them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T08:58:26-08:00","id":1287550,"title":"","content":"Perhaps have the Guild control multiple states via allied (or blackmailed) client kings, have allies with local gods, and have some Outcaste or even Exigent allies for if it comes to a fight. Maybe the Guild factor is a sorcerer with demon bodyguards - though I don't think having a mortal villain is impossible, as long as you accept he's not a combat character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T09:01:02-08:00","id":1287552,"title":"","content":"Oh, and perhaps the Guild is selling slaves to the Fair Folk, and so they offer free slaves to the Raksha in return for their help against the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T09:18:59-08:00","id":1287558,"title":"","content":"Another way to handle &quot;Lunars fight the Guild&quot; (or many other mortal organizations, really), is to remember that the protagonists aren't really fighting a single person, even a very rich and powerful one. Rather, they're fighting an <i>institution</i>, and that is considerably harder. It's not nearly so easy to destroy it by killing a single person, or even a lot of people. If they kill one Guild caravan, well, what of it? The Guild takes losses into account in their plans, they'll send another one. If they kill every caravan, well, the destination is probably still profitable, the Guild will find another route, or several. Or they'll buy out all the local caravaneers, so now the party has to choose between leaving locals alive, and continuing their policy of destroying the caravans. If the party manages to get someone loyal to them infiltrated into the local Guild organization, remember that power and money both corrupt - their agent could find they like the good life more than service to the Lunars. And if all that doesn't work, the Guild can and does still <i>hire</i> supernatural beings, even if they try to keep them out of positions of power. Plenty of Exigents, Liminals, Dragon-Bloods, and even Solars might be willing to go up against the Circle for enough wealth, which the Guild can deploy. And gods and elementals can be bought too - just because they don't have much use for human cash, doesn't mean they aren't susceptible to bribery with things that <i>can</i> be mundanely purchased. <br /> <br /> In short, there's a fair amount of things an organization as powerful and widespread as the Guild can do to fight against and even win against beings as powerful as Lunars. I'm not saying the Circle shouldn't eventually win their struggle, but there's absolutely no need to assume it will be a cakewalk for them, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T10:28:56-08:00","id":1287581,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for a stand-in for enlightened essence before the Guild starts recruiting going to supernatural communities for help, that'd be weird pets.<br /> <br /> It's an incentive to have, for example, a merchant prince who drops people who annoy her into a shark tank like a fucking Bond villain. It won't slow the average group of PCs down anymore than having her declare &quot;I know kung fu!&quot; and activate a Terrestrial Martial Arts form would've done, but it's potentially more memorable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:47:04-08:00","id":1287680,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously I never expected a Guild prince or mercenary captain to go toe-to-toe with a Lunar in a climactic battle. But it does feel like if I want combat to be any challenge at all, I'll need to lean heavily on supernatural allies, bodyguards and servants. This is all good advice though, so I'll keep it in mind if I do run such a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:25:00-08:00","id":1288032,"title":"","content":"Some more notes on mortal mercenaries.<br /> <br /> A huge block of infantry with a singular commander is potentially mincemeat against a circle of Exalts, are the troops all the same quality? is there a ranged element? cavalry? who does the commander delegate orders to? Consider local exotic fauna and minor supernatural elements that can be harnessed. Exotic pets can come to the forefront again when they have a siege lizard fitted with a howdah to provide a moving fortress.<br /> <br /> On the smaller scale they might gather up groups of the best mortals they can get on short notice, Zahara the former Bride of Ahlat turned bounty hunter her husband Two-Flame Kid rumoured to be a son of the Tri-Khan driven into exile for scarring his brother in a pointless duel, Ghiberti an exile from his clan of turtle beastfolk who is impressively tough with his reinforced shell and last but not least is Night's Daughter a young woman who performs elegant feats of violence for an unseen patron, the Destroyer who may or may not be real. Individually, none of the four is a match for an Exalt but together they might have a fighting chance. Especially with the right opportunity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T22:55:15-08:00","id":1288177,"title":"","content":"I just added some Shaping Rituals that were specific to Martial Arts and you'd do shape sorcery actions but roll (Stat specific to the Shaping Ritual+MA) instead of (Int+Occ) and you could actually hold onto them instead of doing it for a specific action (they'd all drain after a scene). Then the motes could ONLY be spent on MA charms. All of this is just systems, change out the facade and keep the same scaffolding.<br /> <br /> Also, if you really do want MA to be cool and interesting, you should absolutely get rid of the merit, its a real terrible tax. I also actually got rid of Archery, Brawl, Melee and Thrown, combining them all under MA, with your style determining what you knew how to use and what you had access to but this is getting pretty far off topic. The point being that adding in ways to model out Mortals getting supernatural MA and MA charms is already in the system, you just got switch out some pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23811-taintedbalance","name":"TaintedBalance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:36:58-08:00","id":1288189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1288032#post1288032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some more notes on mortal mercenaries.<br /> <br /> A huge block of infantry with a singular commander is potentially mincemeat against a circle of Exalts, are the troops all the same quality? is there a ranged element? cavalry? who does the commander delegate orders to? Consider local exotic fauna and minor supernatural elements that can be harnessed. Exotic pets can come to the forefront again when they have a siege lizard fitted with a howdah to provide a moving fortress.<br /> <br /> On the smaller scale they might gather up groups of the best mortals they can get on short notice, Zahara the former Bride of Ahlat turned bounty hunter her husband Two-Flame Kid rumoured to be a son of the Tri-Khan driven into exile for scarring his brother in a pointless duel, Ghiberti an exile from his clan of turtle beastfolk who is impressively tough with his reinforced shell and last but not least is Night's Daughter a young woman who performs elegant feats of violence for an unseen patron, the Destroyer who may or may not be real. Individually, none of the four is a match for an Exalt but together they might have a fighting chance. Especially with the right opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can attest to this. I once ran a short mortal game where my players fought and beat many exalted foes. I would even dare to call some of the fights an easy win for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:43:57-08:00","id":1288191,"title":"","content":"Also not every fight is gonna be instances of opponents straight-up throwing numbers at each other until everyone on the other side is dead.<br /> <br /> In my Okeanos game, for instance, Barbus and Seamstress were fighting a mist demon, and the demon got a fairly serious advantage when it used a tentacle to pull Seamstress under the water; Barbus had to stop attacking the thing and use a Disengage to dive in after her.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Hectorae bragged to a mortal sailor crew that he could &quot;slaughter all of you without breaking a sweat.&quot; And maybe he could have, if they didn't punch a huge hole in the lifeboat he was standing in, causing him to sink into shark-infested waters in heavy armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T05:10:20-08:00","id":1288224,"title":"","content":"I point to a scene like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x2qpn4ulIBE\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> for what I want for mortals vs. Exalts. Spoilers for Clone Wars Season 5.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Darth Maul's name is pretty synonymous with badass and four bounty hunters (and a really good boy!) inconvenienced him and lived. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:01:37-08:00","id":1288402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1288032#post1288032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some more notes on mortal mercenaries.<br /> <br /> A huge block of infantry with a singular commander is potentially mincemeat against a circle of Exalts, are the troops all the same quality? is there a ranged element? cavalry? who does the commander delegate orders to? Consider local exotic fauna and minor supernatural elements that can be harnessed. Exotic pets can come to the forefront again when they have a siege lizard fitted with a howdah to provide a moving fortress.<br /> <br /> On the smaller scale they might gather up groups of the best mortals they can get on short notice, Zahara the former Bride of Ahlat turned bounty hunter her husband Two-Flame Kid rumoured to be a son of the Tri-Khan driven into exile for scarring his brother in a pointless duel, Ghiberti an exile from his clan of turtle beastfolk who is impressively tough with his reinforced shell and last but not least is Night's Daughter a young woman who performs elegant feats of violence for an unseen patron, the Destroyer who may or may not be real. Individually, none of the four is a match for an Exalt but together they might have a fighting chance. Especially with the right opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I figure that the opposition would basically have to include a group that, in another time and place, might be the PCs of a long-running heroic mortal campaign. Plus a whole bunch of mooks for a good measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T16:24:44-08:00","id":1288429,"title":"","content":"The degree to which humanity should've been extinct depends on how often you think the average mortal encounters a murderous supernatural entity. The world is so large that, if you don't live near the edge, or within a day's shamble of a Shadowland, your average village can likely go generations without having a serious magical problem drop on it.<br /> <br /> If you do live near the Wyld or a Shadowland, you've probably figured out how to get by under those circumstances - some combination of iron, salt, mortal sorcery, mortal exorcists and <b> diplomacy</b> goes a long way. You may have to leave seven children in the woods every year for the Fair Folk, but you get to live, and the fae won't easily let other powers muck with their farm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:00:18-08:00","id":1288453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1288429#post1288429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The degree to which humanity should've been extinct depends on how often you think the average mortal encounters a murderous supernatural entity. The world is so large that, if you don't live near the edge, or within a day's shamble of a Shadowland, your average village can likely go generations without having a serious magical problem drop on it.<br /> <br /> If you do live near the Wyld or a Shadowland, you've probably figured out how to get by under those circumstances - some combination of iron, salt, mortal sorcery, mortal exorcists and <b> diplomacy</b> goes a long way. You may have to leave seven children in the woods every year for the Fair Folk, but you get to live, and the fae won't easily let other powers muck with their farm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also leaving by a shadowland might actually be to your benefit since dead family members are probably inclined to protect their descendants, holding back some of the worse things that might crawl out of the lands of the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T23:02:01-08:00","id":1289432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286994#post1286994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e, of course, originally presented a five-years-of-asceticism thaumaturgical ritual for becoming an Enlightened mortal, which got me thinking about asceticism-powers-your-kung-fu. One thing that annoyed me about that is how someone could immediately abandon the asceticism after getting the essence pool, giving me the idea that you would have to instead <i>continually</i> adhere to it to recharge you pool. Then I saw how similar that was to the way flaws work in 3e (noting as an incidental bonus that using it as a flaw means that Exalted characters could then use the same code to earn their Solar/Dragon/Lunar/Whatever XP [mechanically justifying the &quot;your essence will be more refined if you adhere to ascetic discipline&quot; idea in a subtle, non-unbalancing way]). Followed by noticing that a flaw approach would support other character types following different ethical ideals, and poking at the 2e Virtue list and then reading some sources about Confucian and Roman ethics.<br /> <br /> Whether it all really works in play I can't say yet, but I love the whole interrelated mechanics-and-setting structure in my mind, down to your mortal supernatural martial artists only going nova when it's important because it takes them time to build it back up.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an idea plot on sufficient velocity, with this in mind. Someone made some kind of thaumaturgy path, with monks eating nothing but chilli, rice, and water. No sex. No wine. With this lifestyle, they build up sucesses, which can be used to do things like chuck fireballs. Break the monk lifestyle? Eat meat? Then your successes start 'bleeding out'. Until you start the lifestyle again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T23:02:01-08:00","id":1289433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1286994#post1286994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e, of course, originally presented a five-years-of-asceticism thaumaturgical ritual for becoming an Enlightened mortal, which got me thinking about asceticism-powers-your-kung-fu. One thing that annoyed me about that is how someone could immediately abandon the asceticism after getting the essence pool, giving me the idea that you would have to instead <i>continually</i> adhere to it to recharge you pool. Then I saw how similar that was to the way flaws work in 3e (noting as an incidental bonus that using it as a flaw means that Exalted characters could then use the same code to earn their Solar/Dragon/Lunar/Whatever XP [mechanically justifying the &quot;your essence will be more refined if you adhere to ascetic discipline&quot; idea in a subtle, non-unbalancing way]). Followed by noticing that a flaw approach would support other character types following different ethical ideals, and poking at the 2e Virtue list and then reading some sources about Confucian and Roman ethics.<br /> <br /> Whether it all really works in play I can't say yet, but I love the whole interrelated mechanics-and-setting structure in my mind, down to your mortal supernatural martial artists only going nova when it's important because it takes them time to build it back up.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an idea plot on sufficient velocity, with this in mind. Someone made some kind of thaumaturgy path, with monks eating nothing but chilli, rice, and water. No sex. No wine. With this lifestyle, they build up sucesses, which can be used to do things like chuck fireballs. Break the monk lifestyle? Eat meat? Then your successes start 'bleeding out'. Until you start the lifestyle again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T03:15:52-08:00","id":1289861,"title":"","content":"Also going back to the idea of making mortal martial artists superhuman.<br /> While I wouldn't go for Evasion 7 I'm not above giving out certain Supernatural Merits as techniques rather than mutations. I mean Earth Dragon style lets you do lethal barehanded which is on a par with having <i>claws</i> so it\u2019s not without precedent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T04:17:26-08:00","id":1289866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TaintedBalance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1288177#post1288177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just added some Shaping Rituals that were specific to Martial Arts and you'd do shape sorcery actions but roll (Stat specific to the Shaping Ritual+MA) instead of (Int+Occ) and you could actually hold onto them instead of doing it for a specific action (they'd all drain after a scene). Then the motes could ONLY be spent on MA charms. All of this is just systems, change out the facade and keep the same scaffolding.<br /> <br /> Also, if you really do want MA to be cool and interesting, you should absolutely get rid of the merit, its a real terrible tax. I also actually got rid of Archery, Brawl, Melee and Thrown, combining them all under MA, with your style determining what you knew how to use and what you had access to but this is getting pretty far off topic. The point being that adding in ways to model out Mortals getting supernatural MA and MA charms is already in the system, you just got switch out some pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We also did this, Mortal enlightened MA as an alternative form of sorcery and it worked well. Besides, if you can learn to draw in motes to power reality altering to create a magical phoenix to blow up shit, why not to power up your kung-fu, right?<br /> <br /> We used sorcerous workings with this for various sorts of training and self-improvement, but most importantly to attune artifacts and unlock/learn charms &amp; evocations . Anyway, it was fun and felt balanced enough. You are still far from the power-level of the actual exalts, but a cut above the norm even if the world is still pretty, pretty scary!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T06:21:47-08:00","id":1289889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1289866#post1289866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We also did this, Mortal enlightened MA as an alternative form of sorcery and it worked well. Besides, if you can learn to draw in motes to power reality altering to create a magical phoenix to blow up shit, why not to power up your kung-fu, right?<br /> <br /> We used sorcerous workings with this for various sorts of training and self-improvement, but most importantly to attune artifacts and unlock/learn charms &amp; evocations . Anyway, it was fun and felt balanced enough. You are still far from the power-level of the actual exalts, but a cut above the norm even if the world is still pretty, pretty scary!</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I just realized something. <br /> <br /> You can create a 'barbarian style' that lets you fight well unarmoured, specialising in broadswords, and fighting superhuman and multiple opponents. <br /> <br /> Then throw against a sorcerer with a dark paramour or demonic initiation. Like a snake demon. <br /> <br /> Tah dah. Conan the barbarian story. Right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T06:33:51-08:00","id":1289892,"title":"","content":"Conan is an influence on Exalted, so I'd be very disappointed if you couldn't do a barbarian vs sorcerer.<br /> <br /> But someone pointed out to me that your point is about a Martial Art.<br /> <br /> And I don't think barbarians are about esoteric and spiritual fighting techniques. Conan is probably better represented by high attributes and abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-20-2019, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:04:50-08:00","id":1289909,"title":"","content":"Aw, that ain't fun.<br /> <br /> I mean..... maybe.... alter it?<br /> <br /> Scratch that. Esoteric and spiritual? Maybe make it so that it's like sorcerous initiation. Lots of different ways to power. All cool. <br /> <br /> That way, you get scholarly men in flowing robes trading blows with naked men with mighty thews","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:15:06-08:00","id":1290774,"title":"","content":"So, Lunar Intelligence charms have a few tricks relevant to this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T23:51:30-08:00","id":1291442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1290774#post1290774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Lunar Intelligence charms have a few tricks relevant to this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please elaborate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:12:05-08:00","id":1291476,"title":"","content":"First off, you can give people mutations, or even turn a whole group into beastmen.<br /> You can also give a mortal the ability to change shape into a specific form (which could even be a different human), but it requires a 4m commitment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:16:07-08:00","id":1291478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1291476#post1291476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, you can give people mutations, or even turn a whole group into beastmen.<br /> You can also give a mortal the ability to change shape into a specific form (which could even be a different human), but it requires a 4m commitment.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Did you read the lunar eugenics thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:44:16-08:00","id":1291482,"title":"","content":"Sadly, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:52:27-08:00","id":1291486,"title":"","content":"Which one? There's been loads.<br /> <br /> That's partly, I think, why the charms* for making beastmen no longer actually involve any, well, sex. One requires you to anoint them with your blood, the other you create a testing ground.<br /> <br /> The testing ground I think has interesting cultural effects.<br /> <br /> *One gives 5pts of mutations based on a certain shape in your Heart's Blood library to one person, the other 6 dots to multiple people.<br /> <br /> A key difference with the old charm for giving people mutations is that they all have to be from one animal. So you are making a beastman, rather than giving them, say, tentacles and wings, or stone skin and talons, or green skin had an insatiable lust for honey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:07:18-08:00","id":1291490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1291486#post1291486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which one? There's been loads..</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234132-wondering-about-lunar-eugenics-2e\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234132-wondering-about-lunar-eugenics-2e\"> Wondering About Lunar Eugenics (2E) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234132-wondering-about-lunar-eugenics-2e\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234132-wondering-about-lunar-eugenics-2e </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, I was recently re-reading MoEP: Lunars, the CoCD: Wyld, and Lords of Creation, and noticed something. Longevity is a Mutation Pox, which can be doubled-down on (for quadruple total lifespan, total 480-510 years, the range dependent on Stamina) by making it into a Blight. It recommends Storytellers require a linked Deficiency (recommending the Diet or the require +25% more food Deficiencies either/or) when dealing with doubled-up Longevity...but this seems like an INCREDIBLY small price to pay for a lifespan that will exceed that of many Dragonblooded. Further, Lords of Creation indicated it was a </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:28:37-08:00","id":1291494,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything preventing you from using multiple instances of Sharing Lunar's Gifts to stack mutations from multiple animals on someone. You just need to wait a story for npcs or for a pc to pay off their experience debt (which I assume they can just do on the spot if they have enough xp to spare) <br /> <br /> The testing grounds charm might be able to stack the same way. Not sure, I dropped an ask about that in ATD a few minutes ago. <br /> <br /> Now, onto some of the points raised in the mentioned thread, aside form the setting being fundamentally different, and in certain societies mutations being a mark of favour because lunars, I would personally see nothing wrong in allowing subtle merits to be granted. That seems perfectly fine. And things like longevity might be possible if the animal the lunar channels is something notably long lived like a tortoise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T05:44:37-08:00","id":1291505,"title":"","content":"Or jellyfish.<br /> <br /> That might be a damned weird society...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T07:00:09-08:00","id":1291522,"title":"","content":"And thus a cool thing to have in your game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T07:06:15-08:00","id":1291523,"title":"","content":"I guess Exalted Healing might be a good way to represent starfish regeneration and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T07:17:21-08:00","id":1291525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1291523#post1291523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess Exalted Healing might be a good way to represent starfish regeneration and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh please. <br /> <br /> We need to make weird societies. Did you know that starfishes can reproduce from a single arm, as long as it has some of the central core?<br /> <br /> Time for a population boom...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T09:43:29-08:00","id":1291553,"title":"","content":"I'm not expecting to see longevity return as a supernatural merit.<br /> It's not good for PCs and when you really think about it - a major aspect of what makes a person 'old' is lasting complications from illness and injury, the majority of which gets removed by Exalted Healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T10:02:40-08:00","id":1291555,"title":"","content":"You don't think a society of turtle people with lifespans comparable to dragon blooded could be interesting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T10:09:40-08:00","id":1291557,"title":"","content":"Tbh, longevity is much more interesting than Exalted healing, which should just be for, well, Exalted, and some monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T12:18:05-08:00","id":1291573,"title":"","content":"Logevity is useful for making really old NPCs. EH is useful on PCs who get into fights","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T12:33:55-08:00","id":1291577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1291555#post1291555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't think a society of turtle people with lifespans comparable to dragon blooded could be interesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm concerned that's world building. You can use it to justify a gerontocracy of hypercompetent methuselahs but the individual turtle person doesn't have an advantage that matters in-game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1291557#post1291557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, longevity is much more interesting than Exalted healing, which should just be for, well, Exalted, and some monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm simply saying that Exalted Healing is closer to what people seem to want from Longevity when you stop and consider what's stopping most people living to 100+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:49:51-08:00","id":1291931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1291577#post1291577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm simply saying that Exalted Healing is closer to what people seem to want from Longevity when you stop and consider what's stopping most people living to 100+.</div> </div> </div> </div>As worded, this is actually really insightful and correct. We die because shit stops healing/repairing correctly. Exalted Healing says &quot;The character heals quickly and perfectly, with no risk of lingering complications.&quot;. That means you stop aging, don't need to worry about most ways we normally acquire cancer, going senile, etc etc. I'd probably rule that as an oversight though, more than something that you should take as intended though. As a 5 dot merit, I'd personally be inclined to it actually extending lifetime as well, but I wouldn't begrudge someone who ruled otherwise. You could take the natural lifespan increase of human -&gt; DB and then use that as a rough formula for anything else. Exalted Healing on a dog gets you a companion for a hundred years, while an elephant will live as long as the DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23811-taintedbalance","name":"TaintedBalance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:32:58-08:00","id":1291955,"title":"","content":"Eh....<br /> <br /> I would also put it as aging gracefully. <br /> <br /> Know those 60 year old men that still do lifts? Yeah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:47:42-08:00","id":1291999,"title":"","content":"Yeah, creation doesn't really run on real world logic like that. Exalted healing will help get you to old age, but it's not gonna extend it very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:49:55-08:00","id":1292000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1291999#post1291999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, creation doesn't really run on real world logic like that. Exalted healing will help get you to old age, but it's not gonna extend it very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answering whom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T16:31:42-08:00","id":1292007,"title":"","content":"Just kinda commenting in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T16:59:23-08:00","id":1292016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1292007#post1292007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just kinda commenting in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.... OK. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I got an idea for a mortal sorcerer. Can I share it here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T18:24:26-08:00","id":1292040,"title":"","content":"I don't know if that's a joke, or why you are asking, but sure. Is this a protagonist or an antagonist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T18:38:58-08:00","id":1292044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1292040#post1292040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if that's a joke, or why you are asking, but sure. Is this a protagonist or an antagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Protagonist write up I made, explaining his origin and backstory. Just for fun. <br /> <br /> Not used in any game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T19:02:02-08:00","id":1292049,"title":"","content":"Aleph, Earthscorpion? I&quot;m going to apologize in advance. I got a story idea, and it just won't go away. <br /> <br /> He was walking along the road.... when the girl fell from the sky. White hair, like silver. Purple eyes. And beautiful beyond belief. A soft tracery of scars and stitches on her, that made her look all the more beautiful. She was injured, she was lost, and he took her in, knowing the pleading words she mouthed through cracked lips. <br /> <br /> At his home, he realized what she was. A demon concubine of the local dragon-blooded sorcerer. She said that, due to her very nature and her duty, she is chaste and unable to love any but Kinmaya, her creator. Then he heard the announcement. The one to return the girl who had fled, would be rewarded. Beautiful women, land, power, generalship, tutorship in the occult... all these would be available. Just give up the girl. <br /> <br /> What had happened, was that the dragonblooded had been summoning Aiderea, and holding them in jadesteel shackles, and doing you know what. This particular specimen rolled a natural 20, or the one putting on the shackle rolled a botch. Whatever happened, she escaped, killing guards with fingers that transformed into syringes and scalpels. She escaped, flesh enduring arrow shots and threw herself off the cliff, enduring the crashes and bumps along the way, until she struck the boy. <br /> <br /> The boy now knew that she would never love him. The boy knew that all his dreams would come true if he just handed her over. And looking at the tearing, quivering face of the Sky-Sewn bride, he makes a decision that he will probably regret. He says no. <br /> <br /> The next few days are hectic. The sorcerer searches, sending out demons and elementals to comb over. But they have already left. Or hidden. Maybe they rolled well, or the Unconquered Sun was kinder this time. But anyway, they escaped capture. <br /> <br /> The end of the story kinda ends with them beckoning Kinmaya from Hell. With the Aiderea having Occult 7 and intelligence 3, its... kinda hard, but not impossible. 10 dice. Difficulty of 6/ 7. Add in ritual implements for more dice (story fodder! Run from the guards! Hide! Sneak into the occult lab!) And then, at the end, Kinmaya comes out. It ain't pretty. One angry second circle demon specializing in War, Sorcery, and Lore and moving in for the kill, versus a Dragonblooded sorcerer who's dabbled in melee, and only good in occult, lore, and survival.<br /> <br /> Actually, it wasn't a battle. It was a slaughter. After the last of the guards has been killed and the last of the demons banished, Kinmaya turns to the boy, and offers him a reward. Tutorship, and patronage, from the Meteoric Twins, the Messenger Soul of the Heavenly Inferno. All her knowledge of sorcery, all his for the taking. As thanks. <br /> <br /> And that's how the tale of Blazing Star, sorcerer of the night sky, was born.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KiFHm3wSattNfufEKvp0K9gRcfpDcEAUTbgm4VlW-0I/pub\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KiFHm3wSattNfufEKvp0K9gRcfpDcEAUTbgm4VlW-0I/pub\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KiFHm3wSattNfufEKvp0K9gRcfpDcEAUTbgm4VlW-0I/pub\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KiFHm3wSattNfufEKvp0K9gRcfpDcEAUTbgm4VlW-0I/pub </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T04:04:17-08:00","id":1295007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1291999#post1291999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, creation doesn't really run on real world logic like that. Exalted healing will help get you to old age, but it's not gonna extend it very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted Healing has a lot of implications that aren't really thought out, yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T04:10:18-08:00","id":1295011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1295007#post1295007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted Healing has a lot of implications that aren't really thought out, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look. Its an rpg. Its not meant to be simulationist. <br /> <br /> Well, at least I don't think it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T12:05:22-07:00","id":1295600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1295011#post1295011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look. Its an rpg. Its not meant to be simulationist.<br /> <br /> Well, at least I don't think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They might not intend to, but they do have a lot of hooks for it being simulationist. I also, philosophically, don't think you can really divorce simulationism from a crunchy RPG - they just have too much ideological overlap. Many of the games systems such as crafting, leadership projects, disease and poison, etc., are explicitly simulationist. The combat system is trying to capture (aka, simulate) a very specific feel of dramatic combat. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, as humans, we assume everything that isn't explicitly otherwise stated, to generally work how it does in the real world, because we don't really have a choice. This is one of the great double-sided things about writing - people's brains will fill in blanks. And we do this based off our prior experience, so assuming that unless stated otherwise that things generally follow &quot;real world&quot; physics and the like is not only the default, its the only rational direction to take otherwise every session will break down into figuring out the logistics of how the world operates and what that implies for any actions you'd take. You can't have your cake and eat it to - if you're relying on your audience being able to fill in the blanks, you have to assume that unless stated otherwise, we're operating on real world logic.<br /> <br /> All Exalted have preternaturally long life spans. No mechanism for this is explicitly given. All Exalted get Exalted Healing for free. Exalted Healing says &quot;The character heals quickly and perfectly, with no risk of lingering complications.&quot;. Aging is primarily caused by transcription errors during the healing process. Drawing the conclusion that Exalted Healing is the source of this, and then extrapolating that benefit to anyone getting the merit follows. More specifically it is sufficient, if not necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23811-taintedbalance","name":"TaintedBalance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T14:50:23-07:00","id":1295657,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the Exalted Healing Merit could exist at different levels of potency that is below the granularity of the Merit - hence why a Dragon-Blooded only lives for hundreds of years, while Lunars, Solars, and Sidereals can live for thousands. As such, a mortal with the Merit might well still only live <i>somewhat </i>longer than the regular span, especially given the way that even the Exalted tend to have the effects of old age advance rapidly on them in their twilit years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T05:58:00-07:00","id":1295778,"title":"","content":"Exalted 3e is explicitly non-simulationsit if it matters any in this. There's a reason actually why the Golden Rule et al. are the first rules in the Systems chapter, rather than storied away somewhere. They make it clear that the rules <i>don't</i> necessairly reflect the world's workings, and that when things look like they make the setting spiral into things that don't make sense, then the rules are just wrong.<br /> <br /> The Exalted Healing Merit probably means you aren't likely to die of pneumonia, infection, or major bodily trauma. But you'll probably not live <i>that</i> much longer than expected long life for humans. Or atleast, not much longer than fantasy settings often let long-lived humans who are halthy live. This can be chalked-up to that while Creation is like Earth until stated otherwise, the thematics exist for someone who's pretty resilient to damage but ends up dying of old age anyhow. Because aging probably <i>doesn't</i> occur for the same reasons, it just happens superficially enough that it works the same for most cases save edge things that narrative kicks in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T06:28:41-07:00","id":1295786,"title":"","content":"As the person who first brought up Exalted Healing as a life extender, I consider it less simulationist than introducing a different merit for longevity because that's requiring a distinct mechanical effect to show people live longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T06:32:44-07:00","id":1295787,"title":"","content":"Something something life force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T17:29:27-07:00","id":1295985,"title":"","content":"We get a setting chapter filled with all kinds of cool and interesting mortals in 3E, and it turns out that the revival of this thread was predicated on arguing the minutiae of a Merit to contrive an explanation for living indefinitely?<br /> <br /> That's a bummer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T18:56:33-07:00","id":1296004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TaintedBalance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1295600#post1295600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They might not intend to, but they do have a lot of hooks for it being simulationist. I also, philosophically, don't think you can really divorce simulationism from a crunchy RPG - they just have too much ideological overlap. Many of the games systems such as crafting, leadership projects, disease and poison, etc., are explicitly simulationist. The combat system is trying to capture (aka, simulate) a very specific feel of dramatic combat.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, as humans, we assume everything that isn't explicitly otherwise stated, to generally work how it does in the real world, because we don't really have a choice. This is one of the great double-sided things about writing - people's brains will fill in blanks. And we do this based off our prior experience, so assuming that unless stated otherwise that things generally follow &quot;real world&quot; physics and the like is not only the default, its the only rational direction to take otherwise every session will break down into figuring out the logistics of how the world operates and what that implies for any actions you'd take. You can't have your cake and eat it to - if you're relying on your audience being able to fill in the blanks, you have to assume that unless stated otherwise, we're operating on real world logic.<br /> <br /> All Exalted have preternaturally long life spans. No mechanism for this is explicitly given. All Exalted get Exalted Healing for free. Exalted Healing says &quot;The character heals quickly and perfectly, with no risk of lingering complications.&quot;. Aging is primarily caused by transcription errors during the healing process. Drawing the conclusion that Exalted Healing is the source of this, and then extrapolating that benefit to anyone getting the merit follows. More specifically it is sufficient, if not necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, if exalted healing was all there was too it there wouldn't be such a huge difference in lifespan between the various chosen. Even just taking into account the 'classic' splats from the Primordial war Dragon Blodded get around 300 years, Lunars and Solars get about 3000 years, and Sidereals get 5000. Thats a pretty huge difference given they all have the thing you are supposing is the source of their longevity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T19:49:36-07:00","id":1296018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TaintedBalance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1295600#post1295600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aging is primarily caused by transcription errors during the healing process.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an irresponsible statement; the biological foundation of aging remains a matter of speculation.<br /> <br /> It's also not even particularly accurate as a description of the prevailing theories of the biomolecular basis of aging, which are either the accumulation of oxidation of the nucleotides causing gradual breakdown, and an ongoing process of methylation, which is actually necessary to <i>prevent</i> transcription errors.<br /> <br /> I think methylation might be the big one, and it seems to be a kind of evolutionary quid pro quo; it's necessary for complex organisms to have the kind of life cycles that allow them to have extremely sophisticated biological systems, but it's not something that can really be stop doing what it does, and eventually accumulates to such a degree that transcription kind of stops functioning altogether. Or at least enough that the reduced cellular activity causes some other higher level cascade failure, or renders one more highly vulnerable to complications based on diet or environment.<br /> <br /> And you wouldn't really <i>want</i> to stop the biochemical process of DNA methylation, because it plays a very big part in preventing you from getting cancer.<br /> <br /> Perhaps programmed cell death also plays a certain part of it, that being another thing important in preventing cancer; it's better to scuttle a cell in its prime and replace it rather than keep it around long enough to increase the probability of its nucleic acid accumulating errors until it starts replicating when it's not supposed to.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand, these things are only vaguely related to the process of repair for gross tissue damage, at least sufficiently that a premise of healing very quickly and efficiently would not be inextricably tied to a capacity to live meaningfully longer.<br /> <br /> But that's all concerning a not altogether accurate subject of real life. Setting that aside, while I don't personally doubt that basic biology functions in about the same way in the setting, I wouldn't ascribe things related to the mythic or the superhuman to it. When it comes to something like increased lifespan, I'm inclined to think it's a matter of being infused with a vitalising juju, and biology kind of has to improvise to keep up. For Exalted, the enhanced healing is just part of the package, not the mechanism by which they are bestowed their improved life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T06:56:09-07:00","id":1296404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1285472-mortals-in-3e?p=1295786#post1295786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the person who first brought up Exalted Healing as a life extender, I consider it less simulationist than introducing a different merit for longevity because that's requiring a distinct mechanical effect to show people live longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do make a good point that there\u2019s no reason to mechanicize Longevity since it doesn\u2019t impact character mechanics. A power that can grant Longevity, SURE - that has game event impact as a character tool. But the fact that a character you\u2019re playing can live for 200 more years if not killed isn\u2019t really going to give them any mechanical advantage in the course of a campaign, so there\u2019s no reason to make it a purchased merit rather than Storyteller/player fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}